7125,hkustgz-ai-summer-camp-junwei-p2,"# Description

Project 2 Title: Video Classification Using Neural Networks

https://github.com/hkust-aiaa5032/homework/tree/main/hw2

In this project we will perform a video classification task using CNN. 

Abstract:
In this project we will perform a video classification task (10-class classification, 5k samples for training and 2280 samples for testing) using neural networks. 
Original videos and video frames are provided. Starter code are provided. Use all the classic machine learning and deep learning techniques you can think of to make it work well. Hint: feature engineering, ensemble methods like bagging and boosting, 3D CNN, Transformers, multi-modal.
No pretrained models are allowed.


Scoring criteria: 
- Accuracy on the held-out test set
- Need to beat the baseline to get a passing grade
- Beat previous best to get A. See [here](https://www.kaggle.com/competitions/hkustgz-aiaa-5032-hw2/leaderboard).
- Top-1 submission will get A+

The form of the submitted result:
- Submission on Kaggle leaderboard. Will be graded automatically (public leaderboard is calculated with approximately 50% of the test data. The final results will be based on the other 50%, so the final standings may be different. )
- Code and a one-page write-up of what you did
----------------------
# Evaluation

We will use accuracy as the evaluation metric. The submission file should contain the classification labels (0-9) for each video.","# Dataset Description

## Files
*   **trainval.csv** - the training and validation set label 
*   **test_for_student.csv** - the test set with label column(all set 0), it's also a sample submission file in the correct format
*   **test_for_student.label**- the test set without label column, used for CNN_Classifier_test2csv.py
*   **video_frames_30fpv_320p.tgz**- the processed video frames. Under each subfolder, there are 30 images from one video, we use the middle image for classification

## Columns

id - video id
Category - video category",False,True
