7203,preliminary-round,"# Overview

The goal of the Preliminary Round of DSO-2023 is to assess and identify participants with exceptional data science skills and analytical prowess. Through a series of challenging tasks, this round aims to select the most capable individuals or teams who will advance to the main competition. Participants will showcase their ability to interpret complex datasets, apply advanced analytical techniques, and derive meaningful insights, demonstrating their readiness to compete at the highest level of data science excellence in DSO-2023.
----------------------
# Description

Problem Description

This data was collected via a survey on Amazon Mechanical Turk. The survey describes different driving scenarios including the destination, current time, weather, passenger, etc., and then asks the person whether he will accept the coupon if he is the driver. You have to do the following tasks that are given below:
You have to join train features and train labels together.
You have to clean the dataset with the necessary pre-processing techniques.
Find out the features and target column for classification.
Apply some machine learning techniques to solve the problem.
Finally, you have to test your model with some performance metrics with 30% data from your training dataset.
Accuracy 
Confusion matrix
Precision, Recall & F1-Score
ROC AUC
Log-loss
Find the prediction value from test_features.csv file. 

----------------------
# Evaluation

The evaluation section describes how submissions will be scored and how participants should format their submissions. You don't need a sub-title at the top; the page title appears above. Below is an example of a typical evaluation page.

Submission File
ID must be string and Y must be int or float
For each ID in the test set, you must predict a probability for the Y (TARGET ) variable. The file should contain a header and have the following format:

Id,Y
1,0
2,0
3,0
etc.","# Dataset Description

