#Welcome to the Task 2 of the Intro to ML, DL and CV QSTP!
In this competition, you are given a dataset with each columns representing statistical values of air measured at some place. The date and time of measurement also given as features. The target column is a measure of quality of air.

Your task here is to predict the target column using the given features with various ML techniques which we have taught you!

##Evaluation Metric
This is a **Regression problem**, so the chosen evaluation metric is **R2 score** , Know more about R2 score [here](https://scikit-learn.org/stable/modules/generated/sklearn.metrics.r2_score.html).

##Rules
- You can participate in teams of maximum size 3

- Each team is allowed to make 10 submissions every day

- The public leader board is calculated with approximately 30% of the test data. The final results will be based on the other 70%, so the final standings may differ.
