7286,copy-of-prismap-930-python-coding-test,"# Description

This is a Python Test hosted by PrismaP Lab, Intelligent Critical Care Center for OPS positions. 

The project will provide sample datasets for patients with their [creatinine](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Creatinine) test results. 
The goal of the project is trying to annotate the patients who has [acute kidney injury (AKI)](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Acute_kidney_injury) based on provided criteria shown below.

If any of the following criterion is satisfied, we think patient has AKI.

* Current creatinine value >= 4 mg/dl
* Ratio between current creatinine and reference creatinine > 1.5
* Current creatinine - minimum creatinine within last 48 hours >= 0.3 mg/dl and Current creatinine - reference creatinine >= 0.3 mg/dl
> If there is no creatinine within last 48 hours, skip this condition.

* Patient have dialysis within past 7 days.

Three data frames are given. 
1. Patient reference creatinine dataframe. 
2. Creatinine value dataframe.
3. Dialysis time dataframe.

Please implement the codes and generate the result file:

1. For each creatinine, please label if patient has AKI (Y/N). 

The result will contain two columns, one is called `predicted` while the other one is called `id`.  
**Please check the `Evaluation` section to understand the submission requirements.**
----------------------
# Evaluation

The evaluation pages describes how submissions will be scored and how students should format their submissions. You don't need a sub-title at the top; the page title appears above. Below is an example of a typical evaluation page.

---

Submissions are evaluated on **Absolute Error** metric. 

There are two columns expected in the results:

* **Expected**, it can be a float or integer value, 1 to indicate the existence of AKI, otherwise 0.
* **Id**, it will be used to identify the patient and measurement_datetime, please create the column by concating `patient_id` column and `measurement_datetime` column with `_` symbol. 

Ex. patient_id = 1, measurement_datetime = '2022-09-01 19:08:09',  id = '1_2022-09-01 19:08:09'","# Dataset Description

There are three files of data provided:

* reference_creatinine.csv, the file contains the creatinine test results for reference. 
* creatinine.csv, the file contains the creatinine test results for patients with timestamp of measurement. 
* dialysis_time.csv, the file contains the timestamp of [dialysis](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kidney_dialysis) operation.",False,True
7287,predict-of-electric-power,"# Overview

In order to meet the charging needs of users, the construction and management of charging stations have become an important task. Accurate demand forecasting helps managers allocate power resources reasonably, adjust the installation capacity of charging equipment, optimize operating costs, and provide high-quality charging services.



The competition questions will provide historical electricity consumption data and other related auxiliary information of charging stations. Based on this data, participants need to use machine learning, deep learning, time series and other related technologies to establish predictive models to predict the demand for electricity in the future, help station managers make wise decisions, optimize the operation and efficiency of charging stations, and promote the sustainable development of the electric vehicle industry, Promote innovative applications of smart energy solutions.
----------------------
# Description

RMSE:
 $\hat{y},y$

 $\sqrt{\frac{\sum\limits_{i=1}^n(\hat{y}-y)^2}{n}}$
----------------------
# Evaluation

This game uses RMSE as the evaluation indicator.","# Dataset Description

The purpose of this competition is to predict the power of the next 2 weeks using data from previous years.

train_df:This dataset includes data from the past year.
test_df:This dataset is the data to be predicted for the next two weeks.",False,True
7288,ticket-cancellation-prediction,"# Overview

**Dataset Description**

The dataset has information pertaining to passengers who have booked tickets through a website. The column description of few columns is given below.

ID: a unique identifier, not to be used for training or a feature.
ReserveofStatus: The payment status of the customer.
Gender-Male: Indicates whether the ticket belongs to a male passenger or not.
DomesticTravel: Indicates whether the trip is domestic or international.
TypeOfVehicle: Specifies details about the mode of transportation.
VehicleClass: Indicates whether the vehicle is first class or not.
Vehicle: Specifies the type of vehicle.
Cancel: Indicates whether the ticket has been canceled or not.
HashPassportNumber_p: Hashed version of the passport number.
HashEmail: Hashed version of the email address.
BuyerMobile: Hashed version of the buyer's mobile number.
NationalCode: Hashed version of the national identification number.
Cancelled: If it was cancelled or not

The metric used to evaluation will be F1 score.
----------------------
# Evaluation

The submission will be evaluated on F1 score.


## Submission File
