*   **test.csv** - the test set
*   **sample_submission.csv** - a sample submission file in the correct format",False,True
7289,csse4375-assignment1,"# Overview

The goal of this assignment is to build a classifier that can identify hate or non-hate sentences. 
Your task is to build an accurate binary classifier to detect hate or non-hate senteces (0 for non-hate sentences and 1 for hate sentences). 

The 4375train.csv and 4375test.csv contains two datasets for training and testing. Both files contain additional columns that you may need to remove during the data preprocessing stage. Each data item contains its id, sentence, dataset, index, guideline, and label. Based on your implementation, you will eliminate some of the columns (e.g: dataset, index, and guideline columns). 

Please refer to data section to obtain the two datasets.

Note that your classifier should work on data apart from the provided .csv file. TA will test your code on data items that is not provided in train or test files. 

