7409,pmldl-week-10-gnn-competition-extended,"# Overview

In this competition you will be able to solve a graph classification task. 

**Goal:** The intended learning objective: to be able to train and apply graph convolutional neural networks.
----------------------
# Description

In this competition we use a synthetic dataset of graphs with different structures in both train and test datasets.

To solve the task you need to define and train a graph convolution network.

----------------------
# Evaluation

Submissions are evaluated on the classification accuracy metric.

## Submission File
For each id in the test set, the model should predict a class label 0,...,7. 

    ID,TARGET
    2,0
    5,2
    6,1
    etc.","# Dataset Description

The dataset is for Simple graph classification task.

The dataset has eight different types of graphs.

![](https://data.dgl.ai/tutorial/batch/dataset_overview.png)

Dataset contains two files:
* `graph_classification_train.csv`
* `graph_classification_test.csv`

## Columns description

`Train` split has 5 columns:
* `graph_id` - unique identifier of the sample
* `num_nodes` - number of nodes in the graph
* `num_edges` - number of edges in the graph
* `edges_from` - `num_edges` values that specifies start of the edge. Separated by space.
* `edges_to` - `num_edges` values that specifies end of the edge. Separated by space.
* `label` - target category of the graph (value from 0 to 7)",False,True
