7461,innopolis-high-voltage-challenge,"# Overview

The reliability of electrical networks depends on the presence and condition of insulators. The objective is to create algorithms capable of automatically detecting cases where the glass insulator is missing in the strings of disc-type insulators based on RGB images. Visual predictions' outcomes need to be included in the solution.

1. The task is to assemble a dataset for training a detection model with classification based on the required defect class. 
2. Participants are invited to develop a machine/deep learning model capable of detecting cases when disc-type glass insulators are missing in strings of insulators on power lines. 
3. It is necessary to assess the model's quality on the validation set and obtain predictions from the model on the test set.

>The term 'string of disc-type glass insulators' refers to a configuration of two or more suspended insulators designed to flexibly connect power lines in an overhead power transmission system.

**Goal:** The goal of this competition is to develop a computer vision solution that detects the absence of disc-type glass insulators in strings of insulators on power lines. 
----------------------
# Description


The goal of this competition is to develop a computer vision solution that detects the absence of disc-type glass insulators on power lines.

Tasks

1. The task is to assemble a dataset for training a detection model with classification based on the required defect class. 


2. Participants are invited to develop a machine/deep learning model capable of detecting cases when disc-type glass insulators are missing in strings of insulators on power lines. 

The term 'string of disc-type glass insulators' refers to a configuration of two or more suspended insulators designed to flexibly connect power lines in an overhead power transmission system.

3. It is necessary to assess the model's quality on the validation set and obtain predictions from the model on the test and submission sets.
----------------------
# Evaluation

Submissions are evaluated on mean Average Precision (mAP50) between the predicted probability and the observed target

## Submission File

All participants need to generate a .csv file containing information on the file name with defect number (DJI\_0032), their corresponding bounding box coordinates in relative coordinates (from 0 to 1): (center\_x, center\_y, width, height) and prediction confidence(probability)

If you found more than one defect in a single image, simply right all of the coordinates by comma.

For the provided submission data, the competition experts will assess the mean average precision (mAP50) for each object of the class in the task of detecting the absence of disc-type glass insulators in strings of insulators.

On the final day of the competition, all participants must submit their final results based on the provided final dataset. These results will be used to compile the final table available for public monitoring.","# Dataset Description

On the Roboflow platform, there are available RGB images - data on defects in insulators of various types. 

- https://universe.roboflow.com/traincodelablan2/traincodelab/browse?queryText=&pageSize=50&startingIndex=0&browseQuery=true,
