7471,parcial-de-big-data-heart-disease,"# Overview

This database contains 76 attributes, but all published experiments refer to using a subset of 14 of them.  In particular, the Cleveland database is the only one that has been used by ML researchers to date.  The ""goal"" field refers to the presence of heart disease in the patient.  It is integer valued from 0 (no presence) to 4. Experiments with the Cleveland database have concentrated on simply attempting to distinguish presence (values 1,2,3,4) from absence (value 0).  
   
The names and social security numbers of the patients were recently removed from the database, replaced with dummy values.

One file has been ""processed"", that one containing the Cleveland database.  All four unprocessed files also exist in this directory.

To see Test Costs (donated by Peter Turney), please see the folder ""Costs"" 
----------------------
# Description

La variable que ser¨¢ utilizada como medici¨®n del performance del modelo ser¨¢ el accuracy. El valor m¨¢s bajo ser¨¢ la predicci¨®n que realizare sin ning¨²n tipo de procesamiento de la base de datos y utilizando el m¨¦todo Naive Bayes.

La nota 5.0 correspondera al equipo que haya sacado el mejor accuracy. La nota 0.0 correspondera a los equipos que saquen un valor igual o por debajo del m¨¦todo Naive Bayes en mi primera predicci¨®n.
----------------------
# Evaluation

