* Operating Income Before Depreciation: Operating income before accounting for depreciation.
* Operating Margin: Operating income divided by net sales.
* Preferred Stock: Stock with priority over common stock in dividend payment.
* Profit Margin: Net income divided by revenue.
* R&D: Research and Development expenses.
* R&D/Sales: Ratio of R&D expenses to sales.
* ROA: Return on Assets.
* ROE: Return on Equity.
* S/P: Sales to Price ratio.
* SG&A: Selling, General, and Administrative expenses.
* SG&A/Sales: Ratio of SG&A to sales.
* Sales: Total sales revenue.
* Sales Growth (1Y to 5Y): Sales growth over 1 to 5-year periods.
* Sales Variability: Fluctuations in sales over time.
* Short Term Debt: Debt that is due within one year.
* TEV: Total Enterprise Value.
* Working Capital: Capital used in day-to-day operations.
* businessDescription: A brief description of the company's business.
* close: Closing price of the company's stock. This is useful if you need to engineer a feature, e.g. to calculate Sales-To-Price, by dividing 'Sales' by 'close'.
* dividendFactor: Factor determining the dividend payout.
* fiscalDint: Fiscal year distinguishing information.
* floatShares: Number of shares available for public trading.
* outstandingShares: Total shares currently held by shareholders.
* shortInterestFloat: Percentage of float shares held as short positions.
* FinancialSector: Classification of whether the company is in the financial sector.

Target Variables: (training set only, you predict on the test set and submit on Kaggle)

* FinancialRisk: Risk level assigned to the company, based on its financial profile.",False,True
7491,congenital-heart-disease,"# Overview

The purpose of this competition is to develop a more detailed medical image classification model. Because the diagnosis of congenital heart disease mainly relies on cardiac ultrasound examination, the accuracy of cardiac ultrasound is related to the level of ultrasound doctors. In underdeveloped regions, children with congenital heart disease often miss diagnosis. In the diagnosis guide, chest x-ray has a supporting role in diagnosis. We plan to use CXR to assist in the screening of congenital heart disease in underdeveloped regions, but this requires deep learning models to better pay attention to the details around the heart, and it is best to enhance doctors' confidence in the model through attention heat maps.
----------------------
# Description

The data sets provided in this competition are divided into four types: normal group, atrial septal defect group (ASD), ventricular septal defect group (VSD), and patent ductus arteriosus (PDA) group.
----------------------
# Evaluation

This competition uses ROC as the evaluation indicator.","# Dataset Description

Images of each type of congenital heart disease are classified in different folders, and the folder names are the types of heart disease.",False,True
