7509,zero-shot-classification-of-scientific-papers,"# Overview

Goal:
The primary objective of this competition is to showcase the potential of zero-shot learning in the context of scientific document classification. Participants will be crafting models capable of intelligently categorizing a diverse array of scientific papers across various topics. The emphasis lies on the ability to generalize without relying on labeled training data specifically tailored to the target categories.

Key Points:
Zero-Shot Learning: Participants will need to construct models without any prior exposure to labeled data for the target categories.

Textual Data: Leveraging information from abstracts, titles, and other relevant sections, participants aim to achieve effective classification.

Diverse Categories: The competition spans a wide spectrum of scientific topics, reflecting the interdisciplinary nature of research.

Evaluation Metrics: Submissions will be assessed based on precision, recall, F1 score, and other metrics, with a focus on performance in the absence of labeled training data.

Real-World Applications: Successful solutions have the potential to automate document classification across diverse scientific domains, impacting academia, research institutions, and industries.
----------------------
# Description

DatasetDict({
    train: Dataset({
        features: ['article', 'abstract', 'section_names'],
        num_rows: 203037
    })
    validation: Dataset({
        features: ['article', 'abstract', 'section_names'],
        num_rows: 6436
    })
    test: Dataset({
        features: ['article', 'abstract', 'section_names'],
        num_rows: 6440
    })
})
----------------------
# Predicted Labels

This is sample predicted labels.

""Artificial Intelligence"", 
""Suprevised Learning"", 
""Unsuprevised Learning"",
""Computer Science"", 
""Machine Learning"", 
""Natuural Language processing"", 
""Statistics"", ""Mathematics""","# Dataset Description

This unique challenge tasks participants with developing models capable of categorizing scientific papers into predefined topics without the use of labeled training data. The dataset comprises diverse scientific papers, spanning various fields. Key features include a zero-shot learning scenario, textual data (abstracts, titles), diverse categories, and evaluation metrics such as precision, recall, and F1 score. Successful solutions hold promise for automating document classification across interdisciplinary research domains. Join the competition, explore innovative approaches, and contribute to advancing zero-shot learning in scientific document analysis. Best of luck!",False,True
