7527,credit-risk-scoring-with-xgboost2023,"# Overview

 
----------------------
# Description

Financial institutions usually use statistical models to estimate credibility of applicants for a loan. Applicant with the higest risk are declined, those who are appoved can be assigned different available product parameters based on their score.

Using provided data set, create an extreme gradient boosting model, that will serve for assessment of applicants creditbility. Quality of the model will be measured by its separation power - Gini coefficient.

To pass the competition sucessfully, competitiors should reach Gini higher than 52 Gini (equivalent to AUC 0.76) on the public leaderboard.
----------------------
# Evaluation

Performance of the logistic regression model will be measure by its power to separate good and bad clients - Gini coefficient. ## Submission Format For every out of sample application ID (SK_ID_CURR), submission files should contain two columns: SK_ID_CURR and estimated probability of default or its logit transformation (score). The file should contain a header, be in cvs file with comma as a separator. First column is named SK_ID_CURR and the second one SCORE. ``` SK_ID_CURR,SCORE 1111111,0.1 ```","# Dataset Description

Data file data_devsample.csv holds data to be used for development of the model. Binary variable describing if the client repaid his or her obligations succesfully is in column named TARGET.

Data file data_to_score.csv contains data sample to be scored by the model.",False,True
