The train data contains supervised data for CTR prediction of specific time, user and item.

## Your submission should follow the format of the sample submission file: Id , Predicted.
Id - you do not suppose to change/filter/sort.
Predicted - Predict the click probability [0-1].
###Available Features
#### Target item features
target_id_hash - a unique identifier of a specific item
syndicator_id_hash - sponsored items are provided by syndicators (also called advertisers), and a syndicator_id is a
unique identifier of the syndicator of the current item.
campaign_id_hash - syndicators promote campaign which may include a set of items. So each item has a single campaign, and the campaign_id_hash is a unique identifier of the item¡¯s campaign.
empiric_calibrated_recs - the number of views of the current item calibrated
empiric_clicks - the number of clicks on the target item
target_item_taxonomy - 3rd party hierarchical taxonomy of the target
placement_id_hash - Identifies the location in the publisher site in which the ad has been viewed
page_view_start_time
#### User features
user_id_hash - a unique identifier of a specific user
user_target_recs - the number of times the user saw this target
user_recs - total number of items presented to the user so far
user_clicks - total number of items clicked by the user so far
#### Context features
publisher_id_hash - a unique identifier of the source¡¯s publisher
source_id_hash -a unique identifier of the current source
source_item_type - the type of the source item - Text / Photo Gallery / Video etc.
browser_platform - Desktop / Mobile / Tablet etc.
os_family - Windows / Linux / IOs / Android etc.
country_code
region
day_of_week
time_of_day
gmt_offset

# Note:
At the test file, there is a column named 'Id'. This column represents the original Id of the record within the original dataset (not only cold users).
You may use it if you want to.
However, when you are submitting your prediction use the index of the test file as the Id.

# In other words:
pred = clf.predict_proba(test_df)[:,1]
pred_df = pd.DataFrame(pred)
pred_df.reset_index(inplace=True)
pred_df.columns = ['Id','Predicted']
pred_df.to_csv('my_submission.csv',index=False)",False,True
