7551,mlx-stage-1-round-1-predict-students-marks,"# Overview

Welcome to **mlX Regression Challenge**! The exam season is around the corner and we want you to use your machine-learning skills to figure out how a student would perform in an upcoming examination based on data attributes like their grades, demographic, social and school-related features.

**Goal:** Try to predict the scores of the students in the final G3 exam based on the given features.
----------------------
# Evaluation

The evaluation metric for this competition is Root Mean Square error. The goal of the participants should be to minimize the rmse score. Mean Square Error could be easily calculated using the scikit-learn library (in case you are using Python) by using the following code:

``` 
from sklearn.metrics import mean_squared_error
mean_squared_error(y_true, y_pred)
```

The square root of this error is the evaluation metric. It can be described using the formula:

$$
\text{RMSE} = \sqrt{\frac{1}{n} \sum_{i=1}^{n} (y_i - \hat{y}_i)^2}
$$

---



## Submission File
For each ID in the test set, you must predict the marks for the G3 variable. The file should contain a header and have the following format:

    ID,G3
    2,0
    5,0
    6,0
    etc.","# Dataset Description

The dataset consists of a lot  of features to help you train your models. We are mentioning the unintuitive ones. Please ask in discussions, if you still have questions

`Address` - Rural (R) or Urban (U)
`famsize` - denoted by greater than 3 (GT3) and less than 3 (LT3)
`Pstatus` - Parents stay together (T) / Parents are apart (A)
`Medu` - Mother's education
`Fedu` - Father's education
`schoolsup` - extra tuition support
`famsup` - family educational support
`higher` - wants to pursue higher education
`romantic` - is in a relationship
`Dalc` - workday alcohol consumption (1= very low and 5=very high)
`Walc` - weekend alcohol consumption (1= very low and 5=very high)
`G1` - Marks of student in first period
`G2` - Marks of student in second period

**Goal**  - to predict student marks in G3 (third period)

## Files

*   **train.csv** - the training set
*   **test.csv** - the test set
*   **sample_submission.csv** - a sample submission file in the correct format",False,True
7552,11785-hw1p2-s24,"# Overview

HW1P2 Spring 2024
----------------------
# Description

In this competition, you will create a multilayer perceptron for frame-level speech recognition. Specifically, you will create a frame-level phonetic transcription of raw Mel Frequency Cepstral Coefficients (MFCCs). The MLP will learn a feature representation and nonlinear classification boundary. To discriminate between each phoneme class label, cross-entropy loss will be used to minimize the dissimilarity between output logits and the target labels. The loss will be used during gradient descent to update the parameters of the neural network, thereby minimizing the cost function.
----------------------
# Reference Model

Sparse Multilayer Perceptron for Phoneme Recognition
Note: This Is provided as a conceptual reference paper only. It is very old, and the model in the paper performs poorly given our current methods and understanding. It is otherwise a nice paper, introducing the problem of phonetic transcript generation using multilayer perceptrons.
Link: https://ieeexplore.ieee.org/document/5734801","# Dataset Description

train-clean-100: training set
dev-clean folder: dev/validation set
test-clean folder: test set, sample_submission.csv",False,True
