7646,road-extraction,"# Overview

This dataset is part of the DeepGlobe Road Extraction Challenge, aimed at fostering innovation in the area of road detection from satellite imagery. It contains high-resolution satellite images along with corresponding mask images that indicate the presence of roads. The dataset is designed to enable and challenge researchers and practitioners to develop algorithms that can automatically detect roads with high accuracy, facilitating advancements in mapping services, urban planning, and autonomous driving technologies.
----------------------
# Description

The dataset comprises pairs of images:

Satellite images (_sat.jpg): High-resolution images captured from satellite perspectives, showcasing diverse geographical areas with varying degrees of urbanization, natural landscapes, and road types.
Mask images (_mask.png): Binary images where white pixels (value 1) represent roads and black pixels (value 0) indicate the absence of roads. These masks serve as the ground truth for road detection.
The images have been preprocessed and resized to a uniform shape for ease of use in machine learning models. The dataset is divided into training and testing subsets, allowing for a standardized evaluation of road detection algorithms.

----------------------
# Evaluation

Submissions will be evaluated based on the Mean Dice Coefficient, commonly referred to as the Dice score. This metric is instrumental in quantifying the performance of the submitted models in detecting roads from satellite imagery by measuring the similarity between the predicted segmentation masks and the ground truth.","# Dataset Description

The dataset comprises pairs of images:

Satellite images (_sat.jpg): High-resolution images captured from satellite perspectives, showcasing diverse geographical areas with varying degrees of urbanization, natural landscapes, and road types.
Mask images (_mask.png): Binary images where white pixels (value 1) represent roads and black pixels (value 0) indicate the absence of roads. These masks serve as the ground truth for road detection.
The images have been preprocessed and resized to a uniform shape for ease of use in machine learning models. The dataset is divided into training and testing subsets, allowing for a standardized evaluation of road detection algorithms.",False,True
