7653,vortex,"# Overview

This competition encompasses three distinct challenge categories: ""Best Insights from Data,"" wherein participants analyze data to extract the most pertinent information for informing policymaking decisions; ""Best Algorithmic Approach,"" focusing on crafting efficient models for precise predictions; and ""Best Data Visualization,"" which highlights the utilization of sophisticated visualization techniques to present intricate data nuances in an interactive and visually engaging manner. The dataset utilized pertains to trends in heart diseases spanning a 20-year period within the USA. It has been sourced from the official website of the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention (CDC) under the Open Data Commons (ODC) 1.0 license.
----------------------
# Description

The Creative Computing Society (CCS) at Thapar Institute of Engineering and Technology (TIET) proudly presents ""Vortex,"" an electrifying AI/ML challenge as part of its annual tech fest, Helix 5.0. This 24-hour competition will run from February 8th, 2024, to February 9th, 2024. Participants will engage in three distinct challenge categories:

1.) Best Insights from Data : Delve into the provided dataset to uncover profound solutions. They are encouraged to utilize additional publicly available datasets to complement the given data, aiming to derive comprehensive insights that can significantly contribute to informed decision-making by stakeholders.

2.) Best Algorithmic Approach : Explore, experiment with, and assess a diverse array of ML/DL algorithms to develop a model capable of delivering accurate, stable, and consistent predictions for the designated target parameter, leveraging other pertinent parameters for optimal performance.

3.) Best Data Visualization : Harness sophisticated data visualization tools and techniques to transform data complexities into visually captivating and insightful graphs and charts. The objective is to convey key insights effectively to diverse audiences in an interactive and easily understandable manner.




----------------------
# Evaluation



---
The evaluation format for the challenges would be as follows:

1.) Best Insights from Data : The participants will be evaluated on the basis of the overall insights they draw from the data as well as the feasibility, novelty and applicability of their solution in real-time scenarios

2.) Best Algorithmic Approach : Submissions will be evaluated on RMSE(Root Mean Squared Error) between the predicted value and the observed target.

3.) Best Data Visualization : The submissions will be judged on the basis of their insightfulness, interactivity and interpretability 


## Submission Format

1.) Best Insights from Data :  Participants are required to submit a short presentation(maximum 4 slides) describing the overall picture unearthed from data, its impacts, causes etc. as well as relevant recommendations for the stakeholders. In case, participants are using any external dataset/information, they are required to give references for the same

2.) Best Algorithmic Approach : For each index in the test set, you must predict a numeric value for the Data_Value variable. The file should contain a header and have the following format:

    Index,Data_Value
    2,0
    5,0
    6,0
    etc.

3.) Best Data Visualization : Participants have to submit a document containing all their data visualizations drawn from the given dataset","# Dataset Description

**Introduction:**
The dataset documents rates and trends in heart disease and stroke mortality in the United States from 2000 to 2019. It provides county-level estimates of heart disease and stroke death rates.The data is segmented by age group, race/ethnicity, and sex to comprehensively analyse mortality patterns and trends.

**Dataset Characteristics:**
The dataset encompasses mortality rates and heart disease and stroke trends across various demographic groups and time periods. This dataset has been sourced from the official website of Centre for Disease Control and Prevention(CDC),US Government under ODC(1.0) license.

The dataset presents the occurrences of various cardiovascular diseases like coronary heart diseases, stroke, hypertension etc. among people of different age groups, ethnicities and gender in different counties of the US over a period of 20 years.",False,True
