email- tfugprayagraj@gmail.com","# Dataset Description

##About Dataset
This collection of data provides approximations of the percentage of body fat, which were obtained by measuring body circumference and using underwater weighing methods for 252 men. Multiple regression methods can be utilized to forecast the correct body fat measurements. It is challenging and expensive to measure body fat accurately, and it would be beneficial to have simple and inexpensive ways to estimate body fat.

##Dataset Files
The challenge will provide a dataset named 'bodyfat.csv'. To prepare the data for modeling, you will need to use various cleaning and preprocessing techniques. Once done, the data will be divided into train and test sets to train models and determine the best model for predicting body fat percentage.

file - bodyfat-data.csv [Attached in this window]
testing data - bodyfat-validate.csv [Attached in this window]

Below are the listed variables in the dataset¡­

Density determined from underwater weighing
Percent body fat from Siri's (1956) equation
Age (years)
Weight (lbs)
Height (inches)
Neck circumference (cm)
Chest circumference (cm)
Abdomen 2 circumferences (cm)
Hip circumference (cm)
Thigh circumference (cm)
Knee circumference (cm)
Ankle circumference (cm)
Biceps (extended) circumference (cm)
Forearm circumference (cm)
Wrist circumference (cm)
Note
(Measurement standards are apparently those listed in Behnke and Wilmore (1974), pp. 45-48 where, for instance, the abdomen 2 circumference is measured ""laterally, at the level of the iliac crests, and anteriorly, at the umbilicus"".)

These data are used to produce the predictive equations for lean body weight given in the abstract ""Generalized body composition prediction equation for men using simple measurement techniques"", K.W. Penrose, A.G. Nelson, A.G. Fisher, FACSM, Human Performance Research Center, Brigham Young University, Provo, Utah 84602 as listed in Medicine and Science in Sports and Exercise, vol. 17, no. 2, April 1985, p. 189. (The predictive equation was obtained from the first 143 of the 252 cases that are listed below).

##More details
A variety of popular health books suggest that the readers assess their health, at least in part, by estimating their percentage of body fat. In Bailey (1994), for instance, the reader can estimate body fat from tables using their age and various skin-fold measurements obtained by using a caliper. Other texts give predictive equations for body fat using body circumference measurements (e.g. abdominal circumference) and/or skin-fold measurements. See, for instance, Behnke and Wilmore (1974), pp. 66-67; Wilmore (1976), p. 247; or Katch and McArdle (1977), pp. 120-132).

The percentage of body fat for an individual can be estimated once body density has been determined. Folks (e.g. Siri (1956)) assume that the body consists of two components - lean body tissue and fat tissue. Letting:

D = Body Density (gm/cm^3)
A = proportion of lean body tissue
B = proportion of fat tissue (A+B=1)
a = density of lean body tissue (gm/cm^3)
b = density of fat tissue (gm/cm^3)
we have:

D = 1/[(A/a) + (B/b)]

solving for B we find:

B = (1/D)*[ab/(a-b)] - [b/(a-b)].

Using the estimates a=1.10 gm/cm^3 and b=0.90 gm/cm^3 (see Katch and McArdle (1977), p. 111 or Wilmore (1976), p. 123) we come up with ""Siri's equation"":

Percentage of Body Fat (i.e. 100*B) = 495/D - 450.

Volume, and hence body density, can be accurately measured in a variety of ways. The technique of underwater weighing ""computes body volume as the difference between body weight measured in air and weight measured during water submersion. In other words, body volume is equal to the loss of weight in
water with the appropriate temperature correction for the water's density"" (Katch and McArdle (1977), p. 113). Using this technique,

Body Density = WA/[(WA-WW)/c.f. - LV]

where:

WA = Weight in the air (kg)
WW = Weight in water (kg)
c.f. = Water correction factor (=1 at 39.2 deg F as one gram of water occupies exactly one cm^3 at this temperature, =.997 at 76-78 deg F)
LV = Residual Lung Volume (liters)
(Katch and McArdle (1977), p. 115). Other methods of determining body volume are given in Behnke and Wilmore (1974), p. 22 ff.
Source
The information was collected from Kaggle and was originally provided by Dr. A. Garth Fisher who permitted the data to be distributed freely and utilized for non-commercial purposes.

References
Bailey, Covert (1994). Smart Exercise: Burning Fat, Getting Fit, Houghton-Mifflin Co., Boston, pp. 179-186.

Behnke, A.R. and Wilmore, J.H. (1974). Evaluation and Regulation of Body Build and Composition, Prentice-Hall, Englewood Cliffs, N.J.

Siri, W.E. (1956), ""Gross composition of the body"", in Advances in Biological and Medical Physics, vol. IV, edited by J.H. Lawrence and C.A. Tobias, Academic Press, Inc., New York.

Katch, Frank and McArdle, William (1977). Nutrition, Weight Control, and Exercise, Houghton Mifflin Co., Boston.

Wilmore, Jack (1976). Athletic Training and Physical Fitness: Physiological Principles of the Conditioning Process, Allyn and Bacon, Inc., Boston.",False,True
7690,financial-performance-prediction,"# Overview

**Synnax** is proud to present a carefully crafted dataset containing real financial indicators of 2030 publicly traded companies over 11 consecutive quarters. A lot of effort has been put into compiling these statistics and we believe this data can serve as a basis for a wide range of financial analytics tasks, including budget forecasting, financial health, loan default prediction, etc.

In this competition **Synnax** is challenging Kagglers to predict the companies¡¯ financial data points for the last (closest to today) reported quarter. Each quarter in the dataset is represented by 9 financial data points such as `TOTAL_ASSETS`, `TOTAL_LIABILITIES`, `EBITDA`, etc. and the quarter indicator is the prefix (Q0, Q1, ¡­ Q10) where the ¡°0¡± indicates the most recent quarter in the dataset . The target variables are indicated with `Q0` prefix and are only present in the `train.csv`.

## ! IMPORTANT
Please add your contact details and an Ethereum wallet address to your winning submission for collecting your prize. Please refer to this discussion [thread](https://www.kaggle.com/competitions/financial-performance-prediction/discussion/478828) for explanation.
----------------------
# Description

**Financial Performance Prediction** task is highly creative and can be solved as a traditional ML problem with training models on features to predict targets. The dataset is contains a lot of static metadata characterizing the companies, along with dinamics of change of key financial data points across 11 consecutive quarters. 

Alternatively contestants may use a time series approach based on target variables¡¯ values recorded in the previous quarters. 

One may also enrich the training/testing with macroeconomic statistics based on time frames present in the datasets - refer to data_dictionary.txt for mapping of quarters indicators in the dataset (Q0 - Q10) to the actual dates.

**Important**: Synnax has developed a novel approach to predicting the probability of default for private companies working in the `web3` domain leveraging the distributed ML effort provided by many individual contributors independently. This competition is a prequel to the production phase. It shares the type of data individual contributors shall be working with and grows the community - **Synnax will invite all the top performing Kagglers to take part in the production pipeline with monthly profit sharing**.
----------------------
# Prizes

Kagglers shall be evaluated and rewarded along two scales:

## Absolute best

 - 1st place - 20,000 SYNAI Tokens airdrop
 - 2nd place - 10,000 SYNAI Tokens airdrop
 - 3rd place - 5,000 SYNAI Tokens airdrop


SYNAI Airdrop: SYNAI tokens listing is expected to occur at the beginning of 2024 third quarter of the year. Prior to listing the SYNAI tokens, the utility token that is going to power up the Synnax Protocol, will be minted and distributed via an airdrop to the winners blockchain addresses on Ethereum. Important: when submitting your results for the competition, please include your email and ethereum wallet address in the description field.

## Top 25 in the final Leaderboard

The first 25 Kagglers in the final leaderboard of the competition  will be guaranteed a spot in all the upcoming highly incentivized production phase competitions to predict companies¡¯ financial indicators and invited to join the Synnax Lab as Founding Masters. 

# Synnax Lab

Synnax mission is to become the best place in the world where DS interested in challenging their AI skills and applying them in the field of Financial Credit can come together as a community tackling the biggest problems that so far restrained the healthy growth of the private credit market that still functions on a structure and models created in the 70s. Synnax Lab will be the perfect place for DS to learn, improve and do research on the field on Synnax Testnet environment and through regular highly rewarded challenges. Those that will raise up the ranks of Synnax Lab and graduate as Synnax Scientists will be then eligible to put their skills and model at work in Synnax mainnet where they will be eligible to share ? of the revenues of the whole protocol as a payout for their contributions. The best performers that will achieve the rank of Synnax Masters will be eligible to directly contribute to the development of the Synanx Protocol and Synnax product becoming eligible for special revenue shares.
----------------------
# Evaluation

Submissions are evaluated on the [R2 score](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coefficient_of_determination) (coefficient of determination) between their predicted financial indicators and the actual data. R2 score shall be calculated separately for each of the 9 predicted financial data points then averaged.


## Submission File
For each `Id` in the test set, you must predict 9 financial data points. The file should contain a header and have the following format:

    Id,Q0_TOTAL_ASSETS,Q0_TOTAL_LIABILITIES,Q0_TOTAL_STOCKHOLDERS_EQUITY,Q0_GROSS_PROFIT,Q0_COST_OF_REVENUES,Q0_REVENUES,Q0_OPERATING_INCOME,Q0_OPERATING_EXPENSES,Q0_EBITDA
    2,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0
    5,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0
    6,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0
    etc.

Please check the sample_submission.csv for reference.","# Dataset Description

Dataset contains financial data points for 2030 publicly traded companies based on financial reports submitted to [SEC](https://www.sec.gov/dera/data/financial-statement-data-sets) authority EDGAR database over the course of 11 consecutive quarters starting from Q3-2023 (latest quarter indicated by Q0 prefix) and finishing with Q1-2021 (furthest quarter indicated by Q10 prefix).

### The ordering is as follows:
Columns starting with Q0 contain the companys' financial indicators from the latest reported quarter, it is the closest in time statistics reported by companies.
Q1 - is the quarter which went before Q0
Q10 - represents the furthest statistics in time

Each quarter (except for Q0) contains 17 indicators, please refer to the **data_dictionary.txt** for details.

There are 9 targets which represent the latest financial data points for each company. Kagglers need to train model(s) which will map the historical financial performance of the companies¡¯ to their latest financial indicators.

## Files

- **train.csv** - the training set
- **test.csv** - the test set
- **sample_submission.csv** - a sample submission file in the correct format
- **data_dictionary.txt** - detailed data points description

**Please refer to data_dictionary.txt for detailed columns description**",False,True
7691,airbus-finance-ml-basics-workshop-day-1,"# Overview

 Competition Overview
----------------------
# Description

Welcome to the Airbus Finance NLP Kaggle Competition on classifying Twitter comments regarding airlines.

Participants will be provided with a dataset of tweets related to various airlines, along with their sentiment labels (positive or negative)(airline_sentiment_train.csv)
We will process the text using common Natural Language Processing (NLP) techniques
We will train a ML Classification Model
Participants will also be provided with a dataset of tweets without a sentiment label (airline_sentiment_test.csv)
Each team will submit their predictions and see their ranking in the Leaderboard section
----------------------
# Evaluation

The evaluation metric used will be Accuracy: The number of instances correctly classified divided by the total number of instances. In this case our dataset is very balanced (same number of positives and negatives) so this metric is an appropriate one.
----------------------
# Prize

None","# Dataset Description

The Twitter airline dataset is a collection of comments posted by Twitter users about their travel experiences with different airlines. The dataset is composed of a total of 5,313 tweets that were gathered over a period of six months.

Each tweet has been labelled as either positive or negative based on the sentiment of the tweet towards the airline.

The data has been split into training (3,963 rows) and testing (1,350 rows) datasets
`airline_tweets_train.csv` - The training set, we will use this dataset to train our models
`airline_tweets_test.csv` - The test set, we will evaluate and rank teams with this dataset
Columns
`Id` - Numeric Id of the tweet
`airline_sentiment` - Sentiment of the tweet, 'positive' 'negative' or 'neutral'
`airline` - Name of the airline referenced in the tweet
`text` - Content of the tweet
`retweet_count` - Number of retweets performed on tweet
`user_timezone` - Timezone of the user posting tweet",False,True
7692,stock-market-prediction-and-sentimental-analysis,"# Overview

Use Machine learning techniques to evaluate past data pertaining to the stock market and world affairs of the corresponding time period, in order to make predictions in stock trends. Build a model that will be able to buy and sell stock based on profitable prediction, without any human interactions. The model may use Natural Language Processing (NLP) to make smart ¡°decisions¡± based on current affairs, article, etc. With NLP and the basic rule of probability, your goal is to increase the accuracy of the stock predictions.
----------------------
# Description

# Technex

Technex is the annual techno-management festival of Indian Institute of Technology, Banaras Hindu University, Varanasi, India.

TECHNEX - The wagon of the most promising technical event of the nation is Back! Get ready to witness one of the best gatherings of renowned Technologists, Entrepreneurs, Venture Capitalists, Personalities and Thousands of students and participants. TECHNEX gets Bigger, Better and the competition gets tougher as prizes become more bountiful. The perfect platform to showcase your Technical And Managerial Acumen and transform your raw ideas to Success Stories. Put on your thinking hats and gear up for the Asia's oldest Techno-management festival. Keep visiting this page for further updates.

## Data Prophet
