7710,ml-olympiad-machine-translation-french-wolof,"# Overview

This Kaggle competition challenges participants to excel in machine translation from French to Wolof. Participants will work with a dataset containing French text and corresponding translations into Wolof. The objective is to develop robust algorithms or models capable of accurately translating French sentences into Wolof while preserving contextual accuracy and linguistic nuances. The competition aims to push the boundaries of machine translation by improving the quality and fluency of translations from French to Wolof, ultimately advancing the accessibility and usability of language technology in multilingual contexts.
----------------------
# Description

Welcome to the French to Wolof Translation Challenge on Kaggle!

This competition invites participants to showcase their expertise in machine translation by tackling the task of translating sentences from French to Wolof. As the demand for accurate and contextually appropriate translations continues to grow, this challenge aims to push the boundaries of language technology by focusing on a specific language pair that is both linguistically and culturally diverse.

Translating from French to Wolof presents unique challenges due to the linguistic differences between the two languages, as well as the scarcity of resources and tools available for Wolof language processing. Participants will have the opportunity to explore innovative approaches and methodologies to overcome these challenges and produce high-quality translations that capture the essence and meaning of the original French sentences.

In this competition, participants will be provided with a dataset containing pairs of French sentences and their corresponding translations in Wolof. The goal is to develop machine learning models or algorithms that can accurately translate French sentences into Wolof while preserving grammatical correctness, semantic coherence, and cultural nuances.

To ensure the effectiveness and practicality of the translations, participants are encouraged to consider real-world applications such as educational materials, linguistic research, and cross-cultural communication. 

Join us in this exciting journey to advance the field of machine translation and contribute to bridging linguistic barriers between French and Wolof speakers worldwide. Whether you're a seasoned data scientist or a language enthusiast, this competition offers a platform to showcase your skills and make a meaningful impact in the realm of multilingual communication. Get ready to unleash your creativity and linguistic prowess in the French to Wolof Translation Challenge!

Join us in this exciting journey to advance the field of machine translation and contribute to bridging linguistic barriers between French and Wolof speakers worldwide. Whether you're a seasoned data scientist or a language enthusiast, this competition offers a platform to showcase your skills and make a meaningful impact in the realm of multilingual communication. Get ready to unleash your creativity and linguistic prowess in the French to Wolof Translation Challenge!
----------------------
# Evaluation

---

Submissions are evaluated on [BLEU](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/BLEU#:~:text=Invented%20at%20IBM%20in%202001,popular%20automated%20and%20inexpensive%20metrics.) metric, which measures the similarity between the predicted translation and the reference translation. Scores closer to 1 indicate better translations.



## Submission File
For each ID in the test set, you must provide a predicted translation for the corresponding Wolof text. The submission file should contain a header and follow this format:

    ID,Target
    2,Yal na la jig te yeneeni ndam topp ci.
    5,Doomi Senegaal yi fonk seen r¨¦ew ngir ligg¨¦ey bu jaar yoon ak bennoo.
    6,Loolu la?u Le quotidien L¡¯As xibaar ci ¨¤llarba ji.
    etc.","# Dataset Description

