7715,mlnomads-mlolympiad24,"# Overview

Calling all ML Nomads! 
Unfurl your digital maps, sharpen your coding compasses and join us on a crucial expedition across the diverse landscapes of Morocco. Our mission: harness the power of AI to combat drought and ensure this majestic land's water resources thrive.
----------------------
# Description

## The Oasis Shrinks:

From snow-capped Atlas peaks to sun-baked deserts, Morocco's vibrant tapestry is facing a growing threat: dwindling water reserves. Communities struggle, agriculture falters, and the lifeblood of the land dwindles. Traditional methods of monitoring water are slow, resource-intensive, and leave us thirsting for innovation.

## The AI Caravan Arrives:

This is where you, the ML Nomads, come in. Your expertise in machine learning is the key to unlocking hidden water reserves. Join our thrilling Kaggle competition and train a model that can effectively identify and segment water bodies from Sentinel-2 satellite imagery, becoming our digital nomad navigating Morocco's vast terrains.

## Challenge Accepted?

- Data: We'll provide a massive dataset of Sentinel-2 images, each pixel meticulously labeled to reveal the presence or absence of water.
- Your Task: Train a Deep Learning model to automatically ""see"" water with exceptional precision, segmenting it from diverse terrains across Morocco.
- The Goal: Outperform existing methods, achieving the highest accuracy in water segmentation across mountains, valleys, and everything in between.

## The Impact Echoes:

By winning this competition, your model won't just be a trophy. It will become a vital tool for:

- Improved water management: Precise water location data will guide officials in allocating resources effectively, ensuring communities have equitable access to this precious resource.
- Drought forecasting: By analyzing changes in water bodies over time, your model can predict future droughts, allowing proactive measures to mitigate their impact.
- Sustainable agriculture: Farmers can optimize irrigation practices based on real-time water availability, leading to increased yields and reduced water waste.

## Beyond Borders:

The impact of your work won't be limited to Morocco. Your model and the techniques you develop can be adapted to other drought-stricken regions around the globe, creating a ripple effect of positive change.

## Ready to join the caravan?

Sharpen your coding skills, pack your problem-solving spirit, and let's use AI to turn the tide on drought in Morocco. Together, we can create a sustainable future where water flows freely, nourishing communities and landscapes for generations to come.

Remember, ML Nomads, the journey starts with a single step. Let's make it a giant leap for Morocco! ????

## Competition Details:

### Timeline:
Registration Opens: February 29th, 2024
Competition Start: February 29th, 2024
Submission Deadline: April 01th, 2024
Winner Announcement: April 10th, 2024

### Prizes:
Top 1: 
- L-Sized ML Olympiad t-shirt for the lead of the winning team (Morocco Resident Only).
- Additional Prizes

### Data:
Format: RGB Satellite Image + Segmentation Map

Input-Size: 256x256

Access: [Download link](https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/11fhoAbOSGI-SEPXPE9A4POKS6LWe1agp?usp=sharing) or Kaggle access

### Submission Requirements:

- Code and model architecture documentation
- Trained model files
- Competition report outlining approach and results
- Sharing any external data or resources used for building the model

**Failing to provide the above will make you ineligible to claim the prize**

## Join the ML Nomads community:

Link: [mlnomads](https://www.mlnomads.com/)
Discord: [discord](https://www.mlnomads.com/)
Social Media: @mlnomads

Embrace the challenge, unlock Morocco's water potential, and leave your mark on the world with AI!

 #MLOlympiad #MLNomads #Kaggle #AIforGood #SaveMoroccoWater
----------------------
# Evaluation

This competition is evaluated on the mean Dice coefficient. The Dice coefficient can be used to compare the pixel-wise agreement between a predicted segmentation and its corresponding ground truth.

where X is the predicted set of pixels and Y is the ground truth. The Dice coefficient is defined to be 1 when both X and Y are empty. The leaderboard score is the mean of the Dice coefficients for each image in the test set.

---


## Submission File
In order to reduce the submission file size, our metric uses run-length encoding on the pixel values.  Instead of submitting an exhaustive list of indices for your segmentation, you will submit pairs of values that contain a start position and a run length. E.g. '1 3' implies starting at pixel 1 and running a total of 3 pixels (1,2,3).

The competition format requires a space-delimited list of pairs. For example, '1 3 10 5' implies pixels 1,2,3,10,11,12,13,14 are to be included in the mask. The metric checks that the pairs are sorted, and positive, and the decoded pixel values are not duplicated. The pixels are numbered from top to bottom, then left to right: 1 is pixel (1,1), 2 is pixel (2,1), etc.

The file should contain a header and have the following format:


    image_name, rle_mask
    1,1 1 5 1
    2,1 1
    3,1 1
    etc.","# Dataset Description

The task in this competition is to segment water in RGB bands of satellite Images. 

Please note these important points:

- The dataset contains images where the water is not present. Your algorithm should predict no pixel values in these cases.

- To reduce the submission file sizes, this competition uses run-length encoding (RLE) on the pixel values. The details of how to use RLE are described on the 'Evaluation' page.
## File descriptions
- /train/ contains the training set images, named according to img_name.jpg. 
- /train_labels/ contains the training set segmentation map, named according to img_name.png. 
- /test/ contains the training set images, named according to img_name.jpg.
- sample_submission.csv shows the correct submission file format.",False,True
