7819,gdsc-vashisht-ml-hackathon-open-for-all,"# Overview

Put your machine learning skills to the test in this exciting hackathon during our technical fest! We're challenging you to build predictive models for one of the world's most beloved sports - football.

**The Challenge**

Analyze our comprehensive football dataset and develop a model that can accurately predict the outcomes of upcoming matches (win, draw, loss). Our dataset includes:

Team Statistics: Historical results
Match Conditions: Home/away factors
Results: Home(Win,Draw,Loss)

**What You'll Gain**

Real-world machine learning experience
Problem-solving and data analysis practice
Chance to win prizes
Bragging rights among your peers!
Evaluation

**We're looking for models that excel in:**

Accuracy: The percentage of correctly predicted outcomes.
Uncertainty Handling: Can your model adapt to the unpredictability of football?
Efficiency: Resourceful solutions are always a plus.

**How to Get Started**

Form Teams: Collaboration is encouraged! (Optional)
Get the Dataset: 
Build Your Model: Time to get creative!
Submit Predictions: Let's see how you stack up.

**Timeline**

Dataset Release: 16th March 11 PM
Submission Deadline: 16th March 7 PM
Winners Announced: 17th March 10 AM
Don't miss out on this fantastic opportunity to showcase your ML skills!

**GDSC IIITDM RESERVES ALL RIGHTS FOR THIS COMPETITION**
----------------------
# Evaluation

The Evaluation Metric is the **accuracy score** between the Predicted And True Values","# Dataset Description


## Files

*   **X_train.csv** - the training set
*   **y_train.csv** - the true labels of the training dataset
*   **X_test.csv** - the test set
*   **sample_submission.csv** - a sample submission file in the correct format

## X Columns

date:  The date the football match was played (format YYYY-MM-DD).

home_team:  The name of the team playing on their home field.

away_team: The name of the team playing on the opposing team's field.

tournament: The name of the tournament the match belongs to

city: The city where the match was played.

country:  The country where the match was played.

neutral:  This column likely indicates whether the match was played at a neutral venue (i.e., not at either team's home stadium).  (True/False)

## Y Column

result: 0 for a Draw, 1 for a loss to the home team, 2 for a win to the home team",False,True
7820,the-3rd-repss-t1,"# Overview

# Update: The paper submission site is open. Please check the submission details [here](https://repss-w.github.io/Workshop.html).

# Final Leaderboard
![](https://www.googleapis.com/download/storage/v1/b/kaggle-user-content/o/inbox%2F1975390%2F7a8d00a9c765dc68136ea155795b7983%2Ft1_leaderboard.png?generation=1716286602219052&alt=media)

**Updates about the challenge:**
- In the leaderboard, we found that some team names are not registered. You can submit the results on behalf of your team, but make sure to use your team name when submitting your results. If the team name is not registered, the results will be removed.
- Do not use multiple accounts to submit your results. Multiple accounts will be detected by Kaggle Anti-cheating system after the ending of the test phase. If the cheating behaviours are detected by us or Kaggle, your results will be invalidated. (https://www.kaggle.com/discussions/general/125466, https://pytorch-tutorial.readthedocs.io/en/latest/tutorial/chapter05_application/5_1_kaggle/#513-kaggle)
- All teams are fixed by registration and team member changes are not allowed after the team registration deadline. Please follow the LAs carefully, do not share the challenge data in any form outside your teams.

The 3rd Vision-based Remote Physiological Signal Sensing (RePSS) challenge and workshop will be held in conjunction with the International Joint Conference on Artificial Intelligence (IJCAI 2024) on August 3 or 4, 2024.

The 3rd RePSS challenge and workshop covers research topics related to remote physiological signal sensing from facial videos. Facial videos contain subtle facial color change information induced by heartbeats which reveals physiological signals like remote photoplethysmography (rPPG). Extracting subtle physiological signals from facial videos requires robust computer vision algorithms and biomedical signal processing methods.

This year we are organizing The 3rd Vision-based Remote Physiological Signal Sensing (RePSS) Challenge. The information about the 3rd RePSS workshop is on the [webpage](https://repss-w.github.io/).

**This page is for Track 1: self-supervised learning for heart rate measurement using unlabeled facial videos.**

For Track 2: facial video-based blood pressure measurement, please go to the [webpage](https://www.kaggle.com/competitions/the-3rd-repss-t2)

**The top 3 teams will be awarded certificates if the top 3 teams submit papers and are present at the workshop. Please note that the top 3 teams should submit their code to check whether their method is self-supervised.**

**Please note that researchers who 1) previously worked with the RePSS organizing team, or 2) have collaborated/are collaborating with RePSS organizers that have access to the full datasets of OBF or VIPL-HR-V2, can participate in the challenge. Their performance will be shown in the leaderboard on the Kaggle website, but won¡¯t be counted for the final ranking and Top-3 certificate for fairness consideration. We will clarify this issue with concerned teams during team registration via email. Thank you for your understanding!**
----------------------
# Description

**Track 1 is self-supervised learning for HR measurement using unlabeled facial videos.**
*Pre-training stage:*
We have summarized a list of open-source, large-scale facial video datasets include: (a) [VFHQ](https://liangbinxie.github.io/projects/vfhq/), (b) [FaceForensics++](https://github.com/ondyari/FaceForensics), (c) [DeeperForensics](https://github.com/EndlessSora/DeeperForensics-1.0), (d) [CelebV-HQ](https://celebv-hq.github.io/), (e) [DISFA](http://mohammadmahoor.com/disfa/), and (f) [MAHNOB Laughter Database](https://mahnob-db.eu/laughter/). We have checked each of the datasets to confirm that the video quality is suitable for the task, **no ground truth** is available, and the data can be easily accessed online. **You can also use other face video data for pre-training without ground truth.**
 
*Model fine-tuning stage:*
We provide VIPL-V2 datasets built by the organizers¡¯ team. The dataset contains facial videos with ground truth physiological signals from 400 persons.
 
*Test stage:*
We provide a subset of 200 persons¡¯ data from the VIPL-HR-V2 and the OBF datasets as the testing data. The ground truth signals of the test set have never been released in previous challenges.
----------------------
# Schedule

**Important Dates (may adjust later)**
?	20 March   Challenge opening online
?	23 March     pretraining and validation data release
?	23 April    Team register deadline
?	3 May      Testing data release
?	17 May      Final test submission deadline
?	21 May       Challenge results release
?	28 May    Paper submission deadline
?	4 June    Notification to authors
----------------------
# Evaluation

We use root mean squared errors (RMSE) as the evaluation metrics. For Track 1, the RMSE between ground truth heart rates y and submitted heart rates y' is calculated. 
![](https://www.googleapis.com/download/storage/v1/b/kaggle-user-content/o/inbox%2F1975390%2F4ea2c35db45aaa84d01c99a079efee31%2FScreenshot%202024-03-16%20154357.png?generation=1710596643931163&alt=media)
----------------------
# Instruction about test submission

Your submission should be `.csv` file with `ids` and `HR` columns. `ids` is the video file name. `HR` is the predicted heart rate. The figure below shows the submission format. You can download one submission example [here](https://1drv.ms/u/s!AtCpzthip8c9_WOe0lIutXDyt6m3?e=uNDRBZ).

![](https://www.googleapis.com/download/storage/v1/b/kaggle-user-content/o/inbox%2F1975390%2Fd2997a781df9bf375fe33844591eaf7c%2FScreenshot%202024-03-23%20134315.png?generation=1711194208805302&alt=media)","# Dataset Description

**Pre-training data**
We have collected a list of open-source, large-scale facial video datasets as listed below. You can also use other facial video data in the pre-training stage without using GT.

- [VFHQ](https://liangbinxie.github.io/projects/vfhq/)
- [FaceForensics++](https://github.com/ondyari/FaceForensics)
- [DeeperForensics](https://github.com/EndlessSora/DeeperForensics-1.0)
- [CelebV-HQ](https://celebv-hq.github.io/)
- [DISFA](http://mohammadmahoor.com/disfa/)
- [MAHNOB Laughter Database](https://mahnob-db.eu/laughter/)


**Validation data and test data**

The validation data and test data are from the organizers¡¯ teams, i.e., the VIPL-HR-V2 dataset and the OBF dataset. **Two license agreements (LA) and a team registration form must be filled before participants can get access to any data. The documents can be downloaded from [Onedrive](https://1drv.ms/f/s!AtCpzthip8c9_VNLXYZCG5drAPLu?e=2mhwh4).** Please follow the following instructions carefully for preparing the documents:

1). The LA must be signed by a person with an email that affiliated with an institution or company (e.g., xx.xx@mit.edu, xx.xx@microsoft.com ), which means that the person has a fixed position in the institution or company (e.g., a professor from a university, or an employee from a company). Personal emails (e.g., xxx@gmail.com, xxx@qq.com ) are NOT valid. For students please ask your supervisor to sign the LA.

2). One signer can be associated with multiple registered competition IDs, i.e., one professor can sign the LA and multiple students from his/her group can register to the competition.

3). The signer must read through the LA carefully, and only sign the document when he/she fully understand and agree to all the items listed in the LA.

4). **Participants should send ONE email with all the signed LA and the team registration form in PDF format, named as IJCAI 2024 data agreement_track1_Yourname.pdf to Mr. Chenhang Ying (chying@zju.edu.cn), Mr. Jiyang Tang (tangjiyang22s@ict.ac.cn), Dr. Xiaobai Li(xiaobai.li@zju.edu.cn), and Dr. Hu Han (hanhu@ict.ac.cn).** We will send you the download link after receiving the signed LA and the team registration form.

5). The signer is fully responsible (for all users whose IDs are associated with him/her) to make sure that all associated ID users are fully aware of the LA contents, and the data is accessed and used in the proper way according to LA. Data users have no right to distribute the data in any form.

6). The data is shared only for research purpose of this competition usage but not for any other usage. All data must be deleted after the competition by 15.06.2024.",False,True
