The 3rd Vision-based Remote Physiological Signal Sensing (RePSS) challenge and workshop will be held in conjunction with the International Joint Conference on Artificial Intelligence (IJCAI 2024) on August 3 or 4, 2024.

The 3rd RePSS challenge and workshop covers research topics related to remote physiological signal sensing from facial videos. Facial videos contain subtle facial color change information induced by heartbeats which reveals physiological signals like remote photoplethysmography (rPPG). Extracting subtle physiological signals from facial videos requires robust computer vision algorithms and biomedical signal processing methods.

This year we are organizing The 3rd Vision-based Remote Physiological Signal Sensing (RePSS) Challenge. The information about the 3rd RePSS workshop is on the [webpage](https://repss-w.github.io/).

**This page is for Track 2: facial video-based blood pressure measurement.**

For Track 1: self-supervised learning for heart rate measurement using unlabeled facial videos, please go to the [webpage](https://www.kaggle.com/competitions/the-3rd-repss-t1).

**The top 3 teams will be awarded certificates if the top 3 teams submit papers and are present at the workshop.**

**Please note that researchers who 1) previously worked with the RePSS organizing team, or 2) have collaborated/are collaborating with RePSS organizers that have access to the full datasets of OBF or VIPL-HR-V2, can participate in the challenge. Their performance will be shown in the leaderboard on the Kaggle website, but won¡¯t be counted for the final ranking and Top-3 certificate for fairness consideration. We will clarify this issue with concerned teams during team registration via email. Thank you for your understanding!**
----------------------
# Description

**Track 2 is rPPG-based blood pressure measurement.**

*Training stage*
There is a large-scale rPPG dataset (vital videos, https://vitalvideos.org/) with facial videos and blood pressure labels from around 880 subjects. The video and labels in the dataset are of good quality. We have made an agreement with the dataset owner that the dataset can be used for the challenge track. Participants can use this labeled dataset to train models for rPPG-based blood pressure measurement. Participants can split part of the training data as the validation set.

*Test stage*
We will use OBF dataset including 100 subjects. There are 200 facial videos with blood pressure labels. Only the facial videos will be released, and the blood pressure labels have never been released.
----------------------
# Schedule

**Important Dates (may adjust later)**
?	20 March   Challenge opening online
?	23 March     Training data release
?	23 April    Team register deadline
?	3 May      Testing data release
?	17 May     Final test submission deadline
?	21 May       Challenge results release
?	28 May    Paper submission deadline
?	4 June    Notification to authors
----------------------
# Evaluation

We use root mean squared errors (RMSE) as the evaluation metrics. For Track 2, the systolic  RMSE between ground truth systolic blood pressure s and submitted systolic blood pressure s' is calculated first, and the diastolic RMSE between ground truth diastolic blood pressure d and submitted diastolic blood pressure d' is calculated. The final RMSE is the mean of systolic RMSE and diastolic RMSE.
 
![](https://www.googleapis.com/download/storage/v1/b/kaggle-user-content/o/inbox%2F1975390%2F7e81df8b6a3dc02e24cf23f44be30f21%2FScreenshot%202024-03-16%20154221.png?generation=1710596567675632&alt=media)

The organizers will evaluate and rank all teams based on their submitted results. For Track 2, the top 3 teams need to submit their code to us to check whether they use self-supervised pre-training.
----------------------
# Instruction about test submission

Your submission should be `.csv` file with `ids`, `BP_S`, and `BP_D` columns. `ids` is the video file name. `BP_S` is the predicted systolic blood pressure. `BP_D` is the predicted diastolic blood pressure. The figure below shows the submission format. You can download one submission example [here](https://1drv.ms/x/s!AtCpzthip8c9_WCjQ7UZDSNYW2KB?e=8OsJ7k).
![](https://www.googleapis.com/download/storage/v1/b/kaggle-user-content/o/inbox%2F1975390%2Fc9ecab7f3c77b06f85ffa653509bed1c%2FScreenshot%202024-03-20%20171602.png?generation=1710947774908483&alt=media)","# Dataset Description

**Training data**
Please check https://vitalvideos.org/ for the training data information. To access the data, please fill the LA ([download link](https://1drv.ms/b/s!AtCpzthip8c9_WJ2vgT8htcT5npX?e=cdVdF6)) and send it to Pieter-Jan Toye (pjtoye@gmail.com). The dataset has the facial videos, the corresponding GT PPG signals, and GT blood pressure. The owner of the dataset has agreed that only VV-small or VV-medium partitions can be used in our challenge. Please mention you use the dataset for the challenge when requesting the dataset.


**Test data**

The test data are from the organizers¡¯ teams, i.e., the OBF dataset. **The license agreement (LA) and a team registration form must be filled before participants can get access to the test data. The documents can be downloaded from [Onedrive](https://1drv.ms/f/s!AtCpzthip8c9_VeyvZ3r7pWw8Ynh?e=P1ajUC).** Please follow the following instructions carefully for preparing the documents:

1). The LA must be signed by a person with an email that affiliated with an institution or company (e.g., xx.xx@mit.edu, xx.xx@microsoft.com ), which means that the person has a fixed position in the institution or company (e.g., a professor from a university, or an employee from a company). Personal emails (e.g., xxx@gmail.com, xxx@qq.com ) are NOT valid. For students please ask your supervisor to sign the LA.

2). One signer can be associated with multiple registered competition IDs, i.e., one professor can sign the LA and multiple students from his/her group can register to the competition.

3). The signer must read through the LA carefully, and only sign the document when he/she fully understand and agree to all the items listed in the LA.

4). **Participants should send ONE email with the signed LA and the team registration form in PDF format, named as IJCAI 2024 data agreement_track2_Yourname.pdf to Mr. Chenhang Ying (chying@zju.edu.cn) and Dr. Xiaobai Li(xiaobai.li@zju.edu.cn).** We will send you the download link after receiving the signed LA and the team registration form.

5). The signer is fully responsible (for all users whose IDs are associated with him/her) to make sure that all associated ID users are fully aware of the LA contents, and the data is accessed and used in the proper way according to LA. Data users have no right to distribute the data in any form.

6). The data is shared only for research purpose of this competition usage but not for any other usage. All data must be deleted after the competition by 15.06.2024.",False,True
