7827,predicting-contaminated-lakes,"# Overview

**End Date:** 24.05.2024 at 10:00 CET
----------------------
# Description

## Background
The National Lakes Assessment (NLA) is performed by the Environmental Protection Agency of the US government to assess the biogeochemical health of lakes within the US. Data from the 2007 and 2012 NLA reports have been provided. 

## Statement of task

Predict whether there is human waste in the lakes using the various physical and chemical measurements collected in the NLA survey.

## Data Source 
U.S. Environmental Protection Agency. 2007, 2012. National Aquatic Resource Surveys. National Lakes Assessment. Available from U.S. EPA web page: https://www.epa.gov/national-aquatic-resource-surveys/data-national-aquatic-resource-surveys. Date accessed: 2024-03-01.
----------------------
# Evaluation


The evaluation metric for this competition is the [F1-Score](https://scikit-learn.org/stable/modules/generated/sklearn.metrics.f1_score.html). The F1 score, commonly used in information retrieval, measures accuracy using the statistics precision and recall .  Precision is the ratio of true positives \\(\text{TP}\\) to all predicted positives \\(\text{TP} + \text{FP}\\). Recall is the ratio of true positives \\(\text{TP}\\) to all actual positives \\(\text{TP} + \text{FN}\\). 


$$ F1=\frac{2 \times TP}{2 \times TP+FP+FN} $$

The best possible F1-Score is 1 and the worst F1-Score is 0.

## Submission Format
**For every entry in the test set**, submission files should contain two columns: `Index` and `Human Waste`. For the `Human Waste` column, 0=clean and 1=human waste. For the `Index` column, this is the index of the `test.csv`.
The file should contain a header and have the following format:
````
Index,Human Waste
...,...
83,1
84,0
85,0
...,...

````","# Dataset Description

## Files

*   **train.csv** - the training set
*   **test.csv** - the test set

## Columns
Note that the labels ('Human Waste') are in numerical format, 0<-clean water; 1<-water with human waste",False,True
