# Suggested reading

* [Tilmann Gneiting, Matthias Katzfuss ""*Probabilistic Forecasting*"", Annual Review of Statistics and Its Application **vol. 1** pages 125-151 (2014)](https://doi.org/10.1146/annurev-statistics-062713-085831)
* [Hristos Tyralis, and Georgia Papacharalampous ""*A review of predictive uncertainty estimation with machine learning*"", Artificial Intelligence Review **vol. 57** article 94 (2024)](https://doi.org/10.1007/s10462-023-10698-8)
* [Chen Xu, Yao Xie ""*Conformal prediction for time series*"", arXiv:2010.09107 (2023)](https://arxiv.org/pdf/2010.09107.pdf)
* [Zitong Yang, Emmanuel Cand¨¨s, Lihua Lei ""*Bellman Conformal Inference: Calibrating Prediction Intervals For Time Series*"", arXiv:2402.05203 (2024)](https://arxiv.org/pdf/2402.05203.pdf)

as well as the extensive collection of material in the [Awesome Conformal Prediction: Papers Time Series](https://github.com/valeman/awesome-conformal-prediction?tab=readme-ov-file#papers-time-series) section

**Books**

* [Valeriy Manokhin ""*Practical Guide to Applied Conformal Prediction*"", Packt Publishing (2023)](https://www.packtpub.com/product/practical-guide-to-applied-conformal-prediction/9781805122760) (Chapter 8)
* [Rob J. Hyndman, and George Athanasopoulos ""*Forecasting: Principles and Practice*"", 3rd Edition (2021)](https://otexts.com/fpp3/) (¡ì5.9 Evaluating distributional forecast accuracy)
* [Manu Joseph ""*Modern Time Series Forecasting with Python*"", Packt Publishing (2022)](https://www.packtpub.com/product/modern-time-series-forecasting-with-python/9781803246802) (Note: does not cover probabilistic forecasting)
* [Vitor Cerqueira, Lu¨ªs Roque ""*Deep Learning for Time Series Cookbook*"" Packt Publishing (2024)](https://www.packtpub.com/product/deep-learning-for-time-series-cookbook/9781805129233) (Chapter 7)

**Blogs**
* [Leonidas Tsaprounis ""*Metrics for Distributional Forecasts*"", Mediun (2023)](https://medium.com/trusted-data-science-haleon/metrics-for-distributional-forecasts-60e156c60177)
----------------------
# Prizes

Thanks to the generosity of both [**NannyML**](https://www.nannyml.com/) and [**Valeriy Manokhin, PhD, MBA, CQF**](https://www.linkedin.com/in/valeriy-manokhin-phd-mba-cqf-704731236/) this competition has a [wonderful selection of prizes](https://www.kaggle.com/competitions/probabilistic-forecasting-i-temperature/discussion/493217).

These respective prizes will be awarded by, and administrated by, [**NannyML**](https://www.nannyml.com/) and [**Valeriy Manokhin, PhD, MBA, CQF**](https://www.linkedin.com/in/valeriy-manokhin-phd-mba-cqf-704731236/).","# Dataset Description

This competition dataset consists of a single  time series. There are 64,320 rows of training data spanning from **2016-07-01** to **2018-05-01**. There are 5,360 rows of data in the `test` dataset, spanning from **2018-05-02** to **2018-06-26**. The data consists of a time-stamp and 6 anonymized features. The target is the **Temperature** column. The **first 28 days** of the `test` data are used for the [Public Leaderboard score](https://www.kaggle.com/competitions/private-pi-ii-probabilistic-forecasting/leaderboard), and the **last 28 days** (`id` 67008 onwards) are dedicated to the Private Leaderboard score, to be revealed once the competition has finished.

## Files

*   **train.csv** - the training set: a time-stamp and 6 anonymized features. The target is the **Temperature** column. 
*   **test.csv** - the test set
*   **sample_submission.csv** - has an `id` column, and 21 columns of quantile predictions: `0.025,0.05,0.10,0.15,0.20,0.25,0.30,0.35,0.40,0.45,0.50,0.55,0.60,0.65,0.70,0.75,0.80,0.85,0.90,0.95,0.975`

## Dataset credit:
[Haoyi Zhou, Shanghang Zhang, Jieqi Peng, Shuai Zhang, Jianxin Li, Hui Xiong, Wancai Zhang ""*Informer: Beyond Efficient Transformer for Long Sequence Time-Series Forecasting*"", The Thirty-Fifth AAAI Conference on Artificial Intelligence, volume **35**, pp. 11106-11115  (2021)](https://arxiv.org/abs/2012.07436)",False,True
