7878,automatic-speech-recognition-s24,"# Overview

**Attention-based Speech Recognition**

In this competition you will work on a sequence-to-sequence conversion problem, in which you must
train attention-based (transformer) models to transduce speech recordings into word sequences, spelled out alphabetically. This competition is a part of Carnegie Mellon's Introduction to Deep Learning (11-785) course.
----------------------
# Evaluation

You will be evaluated based on the Levenshtein distance between your output sequences and the ground truth sequences for the test dataset of LibriSpeech.

---

## Submission File
For each ID in the test set, you must predict a character sequence.

The file should contain a header and have the following format:

    index,label
    0,string1
    1,string2
    2,string3
    etc.","# Dataset Description

The dataset is given in a similar format to previous homework in this course.

## Subdirectories

*   **train-clean-50** - the training set
*   **train-clean-100** - the training set
*   **dev-clean** - the training set
*   **test-clean** - the training set

## Files

*   `encoder_weights.pth` - reference CNN-LSTM encoder weights",False,True
