7906,slae,"# Overview

Please read this session carefully. Information contained here should be sufficient for your understanding of the competition.

The objective is to process a set of papers and their related relations, determining HOW each paper supports or refutes the relations we have assigned to it. 

This video covers the SLAE Project and the impetus behind the competition: https://youtu.be/8lj10-sW3UU
This video covers technical difficulties you may face particular to this competition and if you are unfamiliar with some of Kaggle's quirks/features: https://youtu.be/zkgbu0D1tzA

A sample notebook is available to get you started: https://www.kaggle.com/code/theinscrutable/sample-notebook
You can edit the notebook to generate your submission or create your own pipeline based on the sample notebook. Please read this notebook carefully for details about the competition, it should have everything you need to deduce the best way to climb to the top of the leaderboard and win the competition.
----------------------
# Description

In Person prizes available at UNC Chapel Hill. Participants can engage in the competition through pipeline building or prompt engineering. The objective is to process a set of papers and their related relations, determining how each paper supports or refutes the given relation. Participants can utilize NLP models for classification or LLMs, with examples including BERT, Longformer, ChatGPT, and Gemini. A reimbursement of $3 for API credits may be offered if you have already used free credits from each LLM service. Please contact the organizers via email if you think this may be necessary.

All details about the competition will be released following the StatQuest event on April 16th. Participants have the flexibility to work asynchronously until April 19th. We may schedule sessions closer to the competition start date for collaborative work. The final work session is scheduled for 5:30 pm on April 19th. The competition concludes on April 19th 7:30 pm, followed by dinner, the announcement of the winners and the prize ceremony.
----------------------
# Evaluation

Evaluated on accuracy according to per relation accuracy. One-Zero encoding: 1  for match, 0 for not match.","# Dataset Description

Dataset cannot be used or distributed outside this competition and the associated Kaggle dataset without explicit permission in electronic or written form. 

## Files

*   **train.csv** - the training set
*   **test.csv** - the test set
*   **sample_submission.csv** - a sample submission file in the correct format

## Columns

*   `json_data' contains json data, each row is a full paper with relations you should classify.",False,True
