7968,team-9,"# Overview

The binary segmented dataset of squirrels comprises a collection of images featuring squirrels that have been segmented into binary form. Each image in the dataset represents a distinct scene where one squirrel is present, and the images have been segmented by hand to isolate the squirrels from the background. In total we labeled 450 images which we then split into train and test sets. We chose to split the dataset with the ratio of 80:20. There are 100 images in the final validation set.
We didn¡¯t perform any augmentation on the dataset since we decided to leave it to the participants.

Dice is used as an evaluation metric

