7974,skin-disease-similarity-prediction,"# Overview

This competition is aimed at figuring out how LLMs can be used in predicting diseases using their pathological features described in words. The challenge is that LLMs are usually not trained well to understand medical terms. But the hope is that perhaps a combination of LLMs may be able to help.
----------------------
# Description

Predicting a disease accurately from the observed set of features can be very hard even for experts since several diseases tend to have similar features. In this competition, we have computed LLM embedding similarity scores for the pathology features of skin diseases which are similar to each other. Now any single model does not seem to be working well for predicting similarity of these features, but a combination may work well.
----------------------
# Evaluation

This is a highly unbalanced dataset, where the negatives are much larger than the positives. So the final evaluation will be based on the F1 score.","# Dataset Description

## Files

*   **train.csv** - the training set
*   **test.csv** - the test set
*   **sample_submission.csv** - a sample submission file in the correct format

## Columns

*   `similarity manual` - output column depicting manual labelling of similarity between diseases by an expert skin pathologist

*   `sbert `?- similarity scores of the pathological features computed using SBERT
*   `llama `?- similarity scores of the pathological features computed using one of the LLaMA models
*   etc.",False,True
