7993,smart-oasis-hack,"# Overview

Welcome to **Smart Oasis Hack!**

**Goal:** Develop a model capable of predicting **building abundance** using satellite imagery!

This Kaggle Competition is the first part of the [Smart Oasis hack] (https://www.facebook.com/events/425171790034101). Participants of this hack should use their results and findings in their application.

## Context
On April 27 and 28, 2024, the Association Citizenship and Sustainable Development (ACDD) Gab¨¨s is organizing the first Hackathon to safeguard the oasis, for the benefit of 40 young university students.
The aim is to develop a technological solution to detect damage to the Gab¨¨s oasis (uncontrolled construction, damage to date palms: uprooting, fire, etc.), which has become frequent, difficult to identify and threatens the very existence of the oasis.
The solutions developed will help the relevant authorities (town councils, Ministry of Agriculture, etc.) to identify these infringements in good time and rigorously enforce the law. They will also provide the basis for supporting young IT developers in preparing to set up their future companies.
----------------------
# Organization Team

## Association for Citizenship and Sustainable Development Gab¨¦s (ACDD)
![](https://www.googleapis.com/download/storage/v1/b/kaggle-user-content/o/inbox%2F5581038%2Fb271b60ad56b9c42ad575b7149ed7487%2FACDD-gabes.jpg?generation=1713781725697292&alt=media)
ACDD Gabes Tunisia is an NGO that works in the field of sustainable development and citizenship targeting mainly vulnerable territories in southern Tunisia (Oasis, mountains, arid and desert areas, wetlands, ...) affected remarkably by the effects of desertification and climate change (CC).

ACDD is a member of several networks and dynamics of the civil society such as Network for the sustainable Development of the oasis (RADDO), Voice for Climate Action (VCA), National forum for climate Adaptation and that constitute platforms for the exchange of experiences with other associations in Tunisia and in the world to organize and carry out advocacy on common causes.


## African Association for Geospatial Development (AGEOS)
![](https://www.googleapis.com/download/storage/v1/b/kaggle-user-content/o/inbox%2F5581038%2F25d05c63bd5d3987cf70abf69216a9f4%2F93ac9fb5-6a4e-4d66-ba73-e986ff868f9c.png?generation=1713781907267850&alt=media) 
AGEOS is a 7-year scientific association, that is open, inclusive and influent in the geosptail sector with an African reach. AGEOS aims to bring together students, academic, public, and private players in the geospatial field to promote the use of geodata, geospatial, and space technologies for socio-economic development in Tunisia and Africa. Its technical expertise covers geomatics, GIS, Field collection, topography, Drone services, and GeoAI.

AGEOS priorities are on opengeodata with its first Tunisian dedicated portal opengeodata.ageos.org and OSM community animation, local development and support to municipalities and local NGOs through training and projects and finally, environmental projects focused on climate change.


## Higher Institute of Computer Science and Multimedia of Gabes (ISIMG)
![](https://www.googleapis.com/download/storage/v1/b/kaggle-user-content/o/inbox%2F5581038%2Fd374afd98dc059124cc540f5bebc63d7%2F1630561303975.jpeg?generation=1713921193917689&alt=media)
Established on July 9, 2002, the Higher Institute of IT and Multimedia in Gab¨¨s opened its doors in September 2002. This institution of higher education, affiliated with the University of Gab¨¨s under the auspices of the Ministry of Higher Education, Scientific Research, and Technology, has the following main missions:
 - Providing initial training for high-level graduates in the fields of industrial computing and multimedia.
 - Organizing continuous training sessions and improvement cycles for public and private enterprises.
 - Conducting expertise, applied research programs, and technology transfer initiatives.
----------------------
# Description

The data for this challenge originates from very-high-resolution satellite images that were obtained from [European Space Imaging](https://www.euspaceimaging.com/). It includes **[Multispectral](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Multispectral_imaging) (1.6m resolution)** and **[Panchromatic](https://eos.com/make-an-analysis/panchromatic/) (40cm resolution)** images from two different dates:  **May 2010 and February 2023.**

The satellite images were captured by the **[WorldView-3] (https://earth.esa.int/eogateway/missions/worldview-3)** and the **[GeoEye-1 ](https://earth.esa.int/eogateway/missions/geoeye-1)** satellite.
The multispectral images encompass **four spectral bands: Red, Green, Blue and Near-infrared**. Conversely, the panchromatic images are in **gray-scale.**

The geographic zone in question is an area spanning around the Oasis of Chenini, Gabes, Tunisia.
![](https://www.googleapis.com/download/storage/v1/b/kaggle-user-content/o/inbox%2F5581038%2Ffc009e32e64422da632349e2415be2b4%2FCapture.PNG?generation=1713754033309625&alt=media)

In addition to the imagery, building data were extracted from the **[Open Buildings](https://sites.research.google/open-buildings/)** dataset detailed in the paper titled [¡°Continental-Scale Building Detection from High-Resolution Satellite Imagery¡±](https://arxiv.org/abs/2107.12283). 

Subsequently, the map was subdivided into patches measuring 102,4m x 102,4m each **(64x64 pixels for multispectral and 256x256 pixels for panchromatic images)**. These patchs are assigned a metric, denoted as **Building_Score**, quantifying **the density or abundance of buildings** within each specific patch.

## Building_Score Details
A high Building_Score signifies a patch with a dense concentration of buildings, whereas a Building_Score of zero indicates the absence of buildings within the patch.
The Building_Score was constructed through the following steps:
- Randomly select a patch from the designated area.
- Extract the list of buildings' polygons contained within the patch.
- Each building is characterized by its area and a confidence score (indicating the likelihood of a building's presence, derived from the deep learning model utilized to create the Open Buildings dataset). These values are multiplied to obtain the weighted_confidence.
- The sum of weighted_confidence values for all buildings within the patch yields the Building_Score.
----------------------
# Evaluation

Submissions are evaluated using [coefficient of determination (R2-score)](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coefficient_of_determination) between the predicted value and the observed target.


## Submission File
For each ID in the test set, you must predict the Building Score. The file should contain a header and have the following format:

    ID, building_score
    8JfLv9jw9F,0
    YxlI8TW8dD,0
    B1kV9KtIFS,0
    etc.","# Dataset Description

You have access to satellite data from **two distinct dates: May 2010 and February 2023.** However, it's important to note that **ground truth data (building_score) is only available for February 2023**. Your task is to **train your model exclusively using this dataset**, then **you can apply it to predict on the May 2010 images**. Subsequently, the analysis of the instances where the **model generates significantly different building_scores for the same patch across the two dates** will help illustrate illegal urban changes within the?Chenini?Oasis, such as the appearance or disappearance of buildings over time.

## File descriptions
- **train.csv** - the training set. Includes the ID of the patch and the target variable for the date February 2023.
- **test.csv** - the test set. You need to predict the building_score for same date February 2023.
- **sample_submission.csv** - a sample submission file in the correct format.
- **images_2023.rar** - a rar file containing the February 2023 data, comprising two folders
   - **mul_images_2023** - multispectral images of dimensions (64, 64, 4). Channels 1 to 3 correspond to the Blue, Red, and Green bands respectively, while Channel 4 represents the Near Infrared (NIR) band.
   - **pan_images_2023** - panchromatic images presented as grayscale images with dimensions (256, 256).
- **images_2010.rar** - a rar file containing the May 2010 data, comprising two folders
   - **mul_images_2010**
   - **pan_images_2010**


## Data fields
- **`ID`** - an Id that represents a patch
- **`building_score`** - the target variable",False,True
