7995,renewable-energy-production-forecaster,"# Overview

The aim of the competition is to create a model that is uniquely capable of monitoring and analysing weather data to produce a plant-level production forecast. The model can monitor a variety of data simultaneously: meteorological forecasts, data from sensors measuring environmental and weather parameters, or any data that the competitor believes will refine the forecast.
----------------------
# Description

The provided data includes weather data and some calculated values, but the use of data from any external data source is allowed for the solution.
----------------------
# Evaluation

The performance of participants' forecasting models is evaluated using the mean absolute error (MAE). 

---

It measures the average absolute difference between the predicted values and the actual target values. Unlike other metrics, MAE doesn¡¯t square the errors, which means it gives equal weight to all errors, regardless of their direction. 

## Submission File
For each ID in the test set, you must predict a production value for the kw (kilowatt) variable. The file should contain a header and have the following format:

    ID,kw
    23465,0.0
    23466,13.0
    23467,70.0
    etc.","# Dataset Description

Here is a short version of what data a competitor can work with if they do not use data from other data sources.

## Files

*   **train.csv** - the training set
*   **test.csv** - the test set
*   **sample_submission.csv** - a sample submission file in the correct format

## Columns

* 'start' ¨C date of measurement
* 'kw' ¨C current production
* 'capacity_clipped' ¨C maximum capacity
* 'time_hourly' ¨C hourly allocation
* 'S_d' ¨C direct beam solar radiaton intensity
* 'airmass' - airmass
* 'altitude' ¨C altitude
* 'azimuth' ¨C azimuth
* 'irradiation' ¨C solar radiation on a tilted surface
* 'fold_cos ¨C cosine of the sunlight¡¯s incident angle on the ground
* 'panel_cos' - cosine of the sunlight¡¯s incident angle on the panel
* 'day' ¨C daily allocation
* 'sunrise' ¨C time of sunrise
* 'sunset' ¨C time of sunset
* 'rad_lw_mean' ¨C Long wave radiation
* 'cloud_total_mean' - Percentage of the sky hidden by all visible clouds
* 'temp_total_mean' - Temperature
* 'cloud_high_mean' - Percentage of the sky hidden by high cloud
* 'rad_global_mean'  - Global radiation
* 'cloud_low_mean' - Percentage of the sky hidden by low cloudiness
* 'radNetS_lw_mean', - Surface net long-wave (solar) radiation
* 'cloud_mid_mean' - Percentage of the sky hidden by medium cloud
* 'radNetS_sw_mean' - Surface net short-wave (solar) radiation (https://codes.ecmwf.int/grib/param-db/210)",False,True
