----------------------
# Evaluation

## Evaluation metrics

The evaluation of results utilizes the object-wise F1-score. As depicted in Figure 1, the criteria for a correctly extracted building are presented, where the ground truth (GT) is represented by the blue polygon, and the extracted footprint by the yellow polygon. The True Positive (TP) is determined through the Intersection over Union (IoU) of these two polygons, specifically, the ratio of their overlapping area to their combined area, as illustrated in Figure 1a. A prediction is deemed accurate if the IoU between the two polygons is 0.5 or higher, as demonstrated in Figure 1c. Conversely, an IoU below 0.5, or the absence of a corresponding GT, is classified as a wrong extraction (False Negative, FN). Additionally, any overlooked extracted building is categorized as a False Positive (FP). The F1 score can then be calculated based on the quantities of TP, FN, and FP, according to equation below. Ultimately, the team that achieves the highest F1 score, based on the average evaluation result of test set without weight, will be declared the winner of the competition.

Precision = TP / (TP + FP)
Recall = TP / (TP + FN)
F1 = 2 * Recall * Precision / (Recall + Precision)

![](https://www.googleapis.com/download/storage/v1/b/kaggle-user-content/o/inbox%2F4876373%2Fe48685a5e72ee69a7dd45f0de47c4128%2F1.png?generation=1713959053396214&alt=media)
Figure 1. Schematic representation of evaluation criteria for correctly extracted buildings.
