8046,vrd-iu2024-tracka,"# Overview


----------------------
# Description

Welcome to the Visually Rich Form Document Intelligence and Understanding Kaggle competition! This competition is the sub-activity of **The Second Competition on Visually Rich Document Intelligence and Understanding (VRDIU)** in conjunction with the **33rd International Joint Conference on Artificial Intelligence (IJCAI 2024)** in **Jeju, Korea**. Please visit the VRDIU [competition website](https://doc-iu.github.io/) for a detailed competition schedule and important dates. The objective of this exciting competition is to develop a cutting-edge model that takes as inputs a natural language question and a collection of Regions of Interest (RoIs) representing document layout components of the entire document. The challenge lies in training your model to accurately predict the index(es) of the RoI(s) that can provide the correct answers to the given questions.

<img src=""https://www.googleapis.com/download/storage/v1/b/kaggle-user-content/o/inbox%2F6506645%2F6e7c9ad1e83e944fdb5aca4eb1d2815c%2Ftrack_a.png?generation=1712377807355325&alt=media"" width = ""70%"" style=""display: block; margin: 0 auto"" />

The dataset used in this competition, derived from Task B of Form-NLU Dataset ([accepted by SIGIR 2023](https://dl.acm.org/doi/10.1145/3539618.3591886)), sets a new challenge of evaluating whether the proposed models could comprehensively understand designers' intentions and user uncertainties to extract valuable information from input forms. Different from [Visually Rich Form Document Understanding-Track B](https://www.kaggle.com/competitions/dociu-form-nlu-2024-track-2/overview), given key text information, a document image and a set of ground truth \\(RoIs\\), users must develop a non-heuristic retriever to extract the target form components based on the given key query. For example, inputting the required key text content ""Company Name/Scheme"", the desired output from the model is the \\(RoI\\)'s index of paired values where we can easily get the text content (""Tinybeans Group Ltd"") from it. The evaluation metric is F1-Score.

We invite participants to think beyond the conventional and push the boundaries of what's possible in document understanding. By doing so, you can contribute to developing innovative solutions with practical applications, such as automated document retrieval, question-answering systems, and intelligent information extraction. Before conducting this competition, please ensure you read and understand the **Rules** of this competition first. Please get in touch with us anytime if you get confused about this competition. **!!Note a strong baseline model is provided for starting this competition!**

Therefore, gather your expertise in computer vision, natural language processing, and deep learning, and join us in this competition. Engage with a vibrant community of like-minded individuals, exchange ideas, and strive for the top spot on the leaderboard. Together, let's push the boundaries of document-based visual question answering and shape the future of intelligent document analysis.

You can scan the following QR code for more details:
