If you have **more questions or inquiries about this competition**, feel free to fill out this [competition QA form](https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSeDvpSBrNkXlQv4lT8tGNdyjwsKYsNqHhN-zMH1tZF-m2egyQ/viewform). Our organising teams will answer your questions within three working days.
----------------------
# Evaluation

We use the weighted F1-score as the evaluation metric for representing overall performance. 
Let:
$$\text{Precision}_i = \frac{TP_i}{TP_i + FP_i}$$

$$\text{Recall}_i = \frac{TP_i}{TP_i + FN_i}$$

$$F1_i = 2 \cdot \frac{\text{Precision}_i \times \text{Recall}_i}{\text{Precision}_i + \text{Recall}_i}$$

The weighted F1-score is:
$$\text{Weighted F1} = \sum_{i=1}^{C} \left( \frac{n_i}{N} \right) \cdot F1_i$$

Where N is the number of samples, C is the number of classes (i.e., the number of types of key_fix_text), n is the number of samples of each class.
