----------------------
# Prize

- The top 3 teams in the private leaderboard will be granted the Official Certification from Google.
- A USD$2000 prize and an Official Certification from Google will be awarded to the Top-1 team in the private leaderboard.

----------------------
# FAQ

You can find the list of common questions for this competition: [**FAQ_GoogleDoc**](https://docs.google.com/document/d/1GVgkA1bUmrtcXaqyi5EzPUeUNdNBI9dB_si6-50eKRY/edit?usp=sharing).
If you have further questions about this competition, feel free to fill out this [**competition QA form**](https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSeDvpSBrNkXlQv4lT8tGNdyjwsKYsNqHhN-zMH1tZF-m2egyQ/viewform). The organising teams will answer your questions within three (3) working days.","# Dataset Description

Our [**Form-NLU**](https://dl.acm.org/doi/10.1145/3539618.3591886)  is a subset of the publicly available financial form data source for [Form 604 (notice of change of interests of the substantial] (https://asic.gov.au/regulatory-resources/forms/forms-folder/604-notice-of-change-of-interests-of-substantial-holder/) collected by SIRCA. It provides the text records of each substantial shareholder notice form submitted to the [Australian Stock Exchange (ASX)](https://www2.asx.com.au/) from 2003 to 2015. To better comprehend the form designer's intentions, we included the twelve most essential form fields. Each form field expects a **Value** from the user, which should contain the specific information being asked by the corresponding **Key** that expresses the form designer's intention.  The statistics of the dataset are shown in the following table.

![](https://www.googleapis.com/download/storage/v1/b/kaggle-user-content/o/inbox%2F6506645%2F4a6559348e7e22bbe38e012926de3d32%2Ftable.jpg?generation=1706681472291138&alt=media)

In Task B, the Key and Value components from distinguished based on the twelve Key intentions, which include: 
(1) Company Name (com\_nm)
(2) Company ID (com\_id)
(3) Holder Name (hold\_nm)
(4) Holder ID (hold\_id)
(5) Change Date (chg\_date)
(6) Previous Notice Given Date (gvn\_date)
(7) Previous Notice Date (ntc\_date)
(8) Class of Securities (class)
(9) Previous Share (pre\_shr)
(10) Previous Voting Percentage (pre\_pct)
(11) Share (new\_shr)
(12) New Voting Percentage (new\_pct)
Key (1)-(2) and Key (3)-(4) ask for the identity of the listed company and the substantial holder, respectively, whereas Key (5)-(12) query the value of the shares being changed. We simply appended the identifier Key and Value separately to the twelve(12) Key names, and created twenty-four(24) labels for the key-value pairs accordingly, e.g., Each key-value pair would produce 2 labels; for example, ""Company Name Key"" and ""Company Name Value"". Based on these different key intentions, we inspected the value patterns to explore the potential noise caused by the diversified user understanding and uncertainty. 

**Note**: We provide the official tutorials ([Data Exploration](https://colab.research.google.com/drive/1IYVHD8Dj735km5sCYd70df8xz7UyY73v?usp=sharing)) for assisting participants to understand the data structure and start this competition easily.

## Files
This dataset consists of three main splits: training, validation, and testing. For each split, we provide a corresponding csv file:.

CSV File: This file contains the name of the image file of the document's page,  the key text, and the label represented by the bounding box coordinates of the \\(RoI\\) in the document. We only provide the answer for the training and validation set to support you in developing a model to predict bounding box coordinates based on the given key text and the image file.

In this competition, participants can use the training dataset for developing their model, and the original validation and testing dataset will be used for leaderboard evaluation.  We offer an [official tutorial](https://colab.research.google.com/drive/1IYVHD8Dj735km5sCYd70df8xz7UyY73v?usp=sharing) to help users quickly understand the dataset format and structure, making it easier for participants to get started with the competition. Here is the link to the tutorial notebook. 

### CSV files
The dataset contains three CSV files containing different splits: training, validation, and testing. Each file contains document IDs (PMCID) and corresponding questions for each item. Note the ground truth answers (global-ID list) are only provided for the training dataset during the competition period. The ground truth for the validation dataset will be made available after the competition has finished.

   *   `train_dataframe.csv`- the training set which provides the questions and corresponding answers. 
   *   `val_dataframe` - the validation dataset which provides the questions and corresponding answers.
   *   `test_hand_dataframe.csv` - the leaderboard testing set 58% for public and 42% for private, including the handwritten and printed documents.

   *   `submission.csv` - a **sample** submission file in the correct format. **Please note that the Label content should be a list of bounding boxes**.

The details of the columns in the csv files can be found in data preview below.


### Image Files
We provide the document images for each data split. Participants can use the PKL file provided information to locate the document images of each target document. Image files can provide additional layouts and visual cues to make the feature representation more comprehensive. 
 
With this dataset, you can explore the challenging task of training your model to predict the correct bounding box coordinates of the corresponding layout component. The provided files are meant to assist you in building a robust and accurate model for this competition. We hope this dataset will inspire creative solutions and foster progress in Form-NLU. Happy modelling!",False,True
