8100,i-lur-news-classification-2024,"# Description

This competition's goal is to apply the machine learning algorithms you have learned in a text classification task. The task is to classify news articles by their topic.

The dataset contains around 12,428 texts from iLur.am, with 7 different topics: art, economy, sport, accidents, politics, society, and weather. A more detailed description is provided in the Data section.

Acknowledgements
The dataset for this competition is taken from paper Word Embeddings for the Armenian Language: Intrinsic and Extrinsic Evaluation. The source of the data is online news website iLur.am.
----------------------
# Evaluation

The leaderboard is formed based on the classification accuracy score. The public leaderboard displays the score only on a part of the actual test data. The score on full test dataset will be available once the competition ends. Submission Format For every text in the test dataset, submission files should contain two columns: Id and Category, separated by comma. The file should contain a header and have the following format: ``` Id,Category 0,3 1,4 2,0 ``` ... A sample submission file is provided in **Data** section.","# Dataset Description

Participants should train their models using the train.csv file, and submit the predicted categories for the texts from test.csv. The submission file should have the same format as the **sample_submission.csv** (i.e. 2 columns - Id and Category). Submissions should contain predicted categories for each text in the test set.

The dataset contains around 12500 articles with assigned category labels, and is split into train and test parts. The training dataset contains around 10000 labelled articles and the test dataset contains 2500 articles without label (the task is to predict these labels). Below is the full list of labels and corresponding topics:

0 - accidents

1 - culture

2 - economy

3 - politics

4 - society

5 - sport

6 - weather

File descriptions:

- train.csv - the training set
- test.csv - the test set
- sampleSubmission.csv - a sample submission file in the correct format

Data fields

- Id - an anonymous id unique to a given customer
- Category - the id of a movie
- Text - the title of a movie",False,True
