8162,ai-lab-10-spring-2024-section-sunday,"# Overview

This lab aims to familiarize students with machine learning concepts through participating in a Kaggle competition. 
----------------------
# Description

Analyze diamonds by their cut, color, clarity, price, and other attributes to predict the price of a diamond based on the characteristics of cut, color, clarity, and carat.

<img src=""https://physics.aps.org/assets/58434729-f278-4bc7-ad3c-faf98d3db26b/e40_1.png"" alt=""Italian Trulli"">

## Practice Skills
<ul>
<li>AI </li>
<li> What is Learning?</li>
<li>Machine Learning Types</li>
<li> Supervised Learning: Regression problems. Classification problems.</li>
<li>Basic regression techniques such as Linear regression </li>
</ul>

## Overview of How Kaggle¡¯s Competitions Work
<ol>
<li>Join the Competition -&gt; Read about the challenge description, accept the Competition Rules and gain access to the competition dataset.</li>
<li>Get to Work -&gt; Download the data, build models on it locally or on Kaggle Kernels (our no-setup, customizable Jupyter Notebooks environment with free GPUs) and generate a prediction file.</li>
<li>Make a Submission -&gt; Upload your prediction as a submission on Kaggle and receive an accuracy score.</li>
<li>Check the Leaderboard -&gt; See how your model ranks against other Kagglers on our leaderboard.</li>
<li>Improve Your Score</li>
</ol>

## Acknowledgements

<a href=""https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/shivam2503/diamonds"">https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/shivam2503/diamonds</a>
