8186,skku-2024-1-machine-learning-third-project,"# Overview

#Description
The dataset includes images of natural scenes. The model should predict the correct label for each image.

Your goal is to achieve high accuracy for the classification problem.



#Evaluation
Your final grading for the first project will be determined according to your public rank, private rank, and a report.

Public rank + private rank: 10 points
Report: 5 points

*The exact details on grading will not be disclosed until the end of semester.


Only 80% of the test data is used for calculating the public rank in the Leaderboard. 20% of data is only used for calculating the private rank, which is accessible after the Kaggle competition is over. You need to create a model that does not overfit on public rank.



#Submission
You can submit the file **5 times a day**, and and submit **2 files for private rank**.

The submission file should include the index and classification result as the submission.csv file attached.

Set your name as **{student ID}_{name}** in the Team section.



#Rules
You can use any external libraries for the model. You are allowed to use any models, including the ones not taught in class.

You can use any preprocessing methods using external sources.

**DO NOT** use any external dataset you find from the Internet.

**DO NOT** edit the labels before and after the prediction.



#Cheating Policy
All instances of cheating will result in a score of 0 for the assignment and will be discussed with the professor for possible further actions.","# Dataset Description

*   **train.csv** - the training set
*   **test.csv** - the test set
*   **SceneImages** - image folder
*   **submission.csv** - a sample submission file in the correct format",False,True
8187,ucsc-cse-164-spring-2024-final-project,"# Overview

In this challenge, you are required to apply the semi-supervised learning techniques on a customed dataset for image classification. The URL to the Kaggle competition is listed below.

https://www.kaggle.com/competitions/ucsc-cse-164-spring-2024-final-project/
----------------------
# Dataset

This customed dataset has 15 plant categories and 120 dog categories in total. The training set contains 9854 labeled images and 22995 unlabeled images. The test set contains 8213 images.

```
dataset
©À©¤©¤ train
©¦   ©À©¤©¤ labeled
©¦   ©¦   ©À©¤©¤ 00000.jpg
©¦   ©¦   ©À©¤©¤ ...
©¦   ©¦   ©À©¤©¤ 09853.jpg
©¦   ©À©¤©¤ unlabeled
©¦   ©¦   ©À©¤©¤ 09854.jpg
©¦   ©¦   ©À©¤©¤ ...
©¦   ©¦   ©À©¤©¤ 32848.jpg
©À©¤©¤ test
©¦   ©À©¤©¤ 32849.jpg
©¦   ©À©¤©¤ ...
