8216,0612-computer-vision-learning-track-1,"# Overview

Classify 70 types of animals in the images.

These images are collected from OpenImages V6 Dataset. 
----------------------
# Description

Welcome to the ""Nature's Finest: The 70 Classes Animal Classification Challenge"" - an unprecedented competition that merges the realms of artificial intelligence and biodiversity conservation into a thrilling quest for knowledge and innovation.

In a world where technology intertwines with our understanding of nature, this contest invites participants from around the globe to harness the power of deep learning to classify animals into 70 distinct categories. This ambitious endeavor not only pushes the boundaries of machine learning capabilities but also underscores the critical importance of accurate species identification in today's era of ecological preservation.

The 70 classes encompass a broad spectrum of fauna, ranging from majestic mammals and vibrant birds to elusive reptiles and fascinating insects. By delving into this intricate challenge, we aim to facilitate advancements in automated wildlife monitoring, enabling more efficient conservation strategies and a deeper comprehension of ecosystem dynamics.

Participants will have the opportunity to contribute tangibly to scientific research, wildlife management, and environmental education. Their models will serve as tools to counteract habitat loss, track endangered species, and foster public awareness about Earth's wondrous biodiversity.

Moreover, the ""Nature's Finest"" challenge fosters collaboration and creativity among AI enthusiasts, researchers, and wildlife experts, sparking interdisciplinary dialogues and forging pathways for future technological breakthroughs. It is through these collective efforts that we can empower humanity's role as stewards of our planet, ensuring a sustainable future where technology acts as a guardian of biodiversity.

Moreover, the ""Nature's Finest"" challenge fosters collaboration and creativity among AI enthusiasts, researchers, and wildlife experts, sparking interdisciplinary dialogues and forging pathways for future technological breakthroughs. It is through these collective efforts that we can empower humanity's role as stewards of our planet, ensuring a sustainable future where technology acts as a guardian of biodiversity.
----------------------
# Evaluation

Submissions are evaluated on [Balance Accuracy Score](https://scikit-learn.org/stable/modules/generated/sklearn.metrics.balanced_accuracy_score.html) implemented with sklearn.","# Dataset Description

Classify the animals in images.
The data is collected from OpenImages V6",False,True
