8225,just-ai-249-machine-learning-lab-competition-same,"# Overview

The ""[Spambase](https://archive.ics.uci.edu/dataset/94/spambase)"" dataset is designed for the classification of emails into spam and non-spam categories. It comprises 4,601 instances, each described by 57 features. These features include a mix of integer and real values (categorical and numerical), providing a comprehensive set of attributes derived from the content and structure of emails. The dataset captures various characteristics such as the frequency of certain words and characters, the length of capitalized words, and other content-based metrics.

The primary task associated with this dataset is classification, aiming to build models that can accurately predict whether a given email is spam or not based on its features.

Dataset citation: Hopkins,Mark, Reeber,Erik, Forman,George, and Suermondt,Jaap. (1999). Spambase. UCI Machine Learning Repository. https://doi.org/10.24432/C53G6X.
----------------------
# Description

you only need to do `pd.read_csv(path)` to read the data.

Example:
```
import pandas as pd

PATH = ""path/to/my/data/train.csv""
train_df = pd.read_csv(PATH)
```
----------------------
# Evaluation

The evaluation section describes how submissions will be scored and how participants should format their submissions.

---

Submissions are evaluated on **F1-Score**.


## Submission File
For each ID in the test set, you must predict a the class (0 or 1) for the `spam` target variable. Where `0`is for **non-spam** and `1` for **spam**. The file should contain a header and have the following format:
| ID   | spam |
|------|------|
| 1093 | 0    |
| 4002 | 0    |
| 4393 | 0    |","# Dataset Description

