8226,simxrd,"# Overview


**Welcome to the SimXRD Competition on Kaggle!**

Spectroscopic data, particularly diffraction data, are invaluable for uncovering detailed information about crystal structures and microstructures, making them crucial in materials discovery. Powder X-ray diffraction (XRD) patterns are especially effective for crystal identification. To accelerate the advancement of crystallographic informatics, we introduce **SimXRD**.  | [**arXiv**](https://arxiv.org/pdf/2406.15469v1)

**About SimXRD:**

SimXRD features a comprehensive dataset of 4,065,346 simulated powder X-ray diffraction patterns, representing 119,569 distinct crystal structures. These patterns are generated under 33 different simulated conditions that mimic real-world variations, providing a robust foundation for developing and testing machine learning models in crystallography.

**Code Template:**

The code templates are available on our benchmark GitHub repository: [XRDBench](https://github.com/compasszzn/XRDBench).

**Competition Details:**

+ **Dataset:** The competition provides a test dataset without labels (testNOtgt_db). 
+ **Objective:** The goal is to accurately identify symmetry groups from the diffraction patterns.
+ **Leaderboard:** The leaderboard is designed to fairly compare the performance of different ML models on the symmetry identification tasks, focusing solely on space group identification.





For more details and to access the dataset, visit our [GitHub repository](https://github.com/Bin-Cao/SimXRD).

**Check SimXRD:**

```
import mlcroissant as mlc
url = ""https://huggingface.co/datasets/caobin/SimXRDreview/raw/main/simxrd_croissant.json""

dataset_info = mlc.Dataset(url).metadata.to_json

# Print basic dataset information
print(""Dataset Name:"", dataset_info['name'])
print(""Dataset Description:"", dataset_info['description'])
print(""Dataset Creator:"", dataset_info['creator']['name'])

# Print file distribution information
print(""\nFile Distribution:"")
for file_info in dataset_info['distribution']:
    print(""- File Name:"", file_info['name'])
    print(""  Description:"", file_info['description'])
    print(""  Download URL:"", file_info['contentUrl'])
    print(""  Encoding Format:"", file_info['encodingFormat'])
    print(""  SHA256 Checksum:"", file_info['sha256'])
```


----------------------
# Description



**Access and Contact Information:**
- The SimXRD home page is [https://github.com/Bin-Cao/SimXRD](https://github.com/Bin-Cao/SimXRD).
- SimXRD is freely accessible after filling out basic information.
- For any inconvenience, please contact Mr. Cao Bin at: bcao686@connect.hkust-gz.edu.cn.

For more details and to access the dataset, visit our [GitHub repository](https://github.com/Bin-Cao/SimXRD).

----------------------
# Evaluation


We will evaluate the classification accuracy of your uploaded dataset.

## Submission File

Your submission file should be a CSV file with two columns: `ID` and `sg`. For each ID in the test set, provide the predicted space group (sg). A template upload file, named `res.csv`, is provided in the data section. Simply replace the `sg` column with your real predictions.

**Example:**

```
ID,sg
1,21
2,43
3,221
4,230
...
```","# Dataset Description




