8352,range-of-motion-detection,"# Overview

Given the 3D position of the shoulders, hips, knees and ankles, the trainee's range of motion (ROM) within the exercise Good Mornings should be predicted. 
- 3D positions have been derived from [Mediapipe's Pose Landmarker model](https://ai.google.dev/edge/mediapipe/solutions/vision/pose_landmarker#pose_landmarker_model)
- Good Mornings look like [this](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=YA-h3n9L4YU)","# Dataset Description

# Training Data
The `train.csv` file contains the dataset to train your models. The **features** are comprised of data describing the position of 8 landmarks:
- `l11`: left shoulder
- `l12`: right shoulder
- `l23`: left hip
- `l24`: right hip
- `l25`: left knee
- `l26`: right knee
- `l27`: left ankle
- `l28`: right ankle
and each of those landmarks has:
- `x`, `y`, `z`: x, y and z coordinates in 3D space
- `p`: probability that the landmark is within the image frame

Thus, for example the feature `l24x` describes the right hip's `x` position in 3D space.

The **target variable (label)** is called `rom` and describes the range of motion (ROM) of the user within the exercise `Good Morning`. It is a float that spans from 0 to 1. 

# Test Data
The `test.csv` file contains the dataset that your models will be evaluated on.",False,True
8353,ml-course-hw-2-classification,"# Overview

**Welcome to the Machine Learning Course from ITU ACM!**

**Your Goal:** For this Homework, your task is to use binary classification to predict a patient's smoking status given information about various other health indicators. Good luck!
----------------------
# Evaluation

Submissions are evaluated on [area under the ROC curve](http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Receiver_operating_characteristic) between the predicted probability and the observed target.


## Submission File
For each `id` in the test set, you must predict the probability for the target variable `smoking`. The file should contain a header and have the following format:

    id,smoking
    159256,0.5
    159257,0.5
    159258,0.5
    etc.","# Dataset Description

The dataset for this competition (both train and test) was generated from a deep learning model trained on the [Smoker Status Prediction using Bio-Signals](https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/gauravduttakiit/smoker-status-prediction-using-biosignals) dataset. Feature distributions are close to, but not exactly the same, as the original. Feel free to use the original dataset as part of this competition, both to explore differences as well as to see whether incorporating the original in training improves model performance.

## Files

*   **train.csv** - the training dataset; `smoking` is the binary target
*   **test.csv** - the test dataset; your objective is to predict the probability of positive `smoking`
*   **sample_submission.csv** - a sample submission file in the correct format",False,True
