8392,iitb-cs-725-1-2024,"# Overview

In this task, you are presented with a synthetic dataset derived from real-world text data, where your objective is to predict target scores using feature vectors generated from neural encoder models. These embeddings have been compressed to reduce dimensionality of the problem.

The dataset is structured with unique IDs, features and corresponding scores. Your goal is to train a regression model on this dataset. This problem is designed to test your ability to work with regression models.
----------------------
# Evaluation

Submissions are evaluated on [MSE](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mean_squared_error) between the predicted score and the target score. Please do not forget to round the predicted score to nearest integer before calculating the test MSE value. You must report the predicted score in integer in the submission file. 

## Submission File
For each ID in the test set, you must predict a regression score for the example features. The submission file should contain a header and have the following format:

    ID, score
    2,3.0
    5,1.0
    6,2.0
    etc.","# Dataset Description

## Files

*   **train.csv** - the training set that has 1 ID column, 64 features columns, and 1 score column
*   **test.csv** - the test set that has 1 ID column and 64 features columns
*   **sample.csv** - a sample submission file that has 1 ID column and 1 score column

## Columns

*   `ID` - definition of example_id
*   `feature_i`?- definition of feature_i
*   `score` - regression score of example_id",False,True
8393,fa-ii-2024-ii-flujos-de-modelos-tradicionales,"# Description

### Contexto de negocio. 

El c¨¢ncer de pr¨®stata es uno de los tipos de c¨¢ncer m¨¢s comunes en hombres. La detecci¨®n temprana es crucial para mejorar las tasas de supervivencia. La prueba de ant¨ªgeno prost¨¢tico espec¨ªfico (PSA)  puede ayudar a detectar el c¨¢ncer de pr¨®stata en etapas tempranas, cuando es m¨¢s tratable. Sin embargo, el PSA no es espec¨ªfico para el c¨¢ncer de pr¨®stata y puede estar elevado en otras condiciones como prostatitis o hiperplasia prost¨¢tica benigna (HPB). 

El ant¨ªgeno prost¨¢tico espec¨ªfico (PSA) es una prote¨ªna producida por c¨¦lulas normales y malignas de la gl¨¢ndula prost¨¢tica. La prueba del PSA mide el nivel de esta prote¨ªna en la sangre y es uno de los m¨¦todos m¨¢s utilizados para el tamizaje del c¨¢ncer de pr¨®stata.

La EPS SaludPorTi, est¨¢ interesado en priorizar la toma de est¨¢ prueba, aumentando la demanda y detenci¨®n temprana del C¨¢ncer de Pr¨®stata.


### Problema de negocio

La empresa ha decidido contratarlos para que construyan un modelo predictivo que permita estimar la probabilidad de que un usuario entre 48 y 60 a?os de edad presente resultados anormales de PSA.

### Contexto anal¨ªtico

Se espera que entrene diferentes familias de modelos predictivos de clasificaci¨®n (SVC con diferentes kernels, Redes Neuronales poco profundas), precedidos por diferentes procesos de transformaci¨®n (normalizaciones, imputaci¨®n, feature engineering, dummificaci¨®n, PCA,  selecci¨®n de features).

La evaluaci¨®n de la calidad de los flujos de modelos predictivos se debe estimar utilizando la m¨¦trica de ROC_AUC.

Expliquen sus ideas, el por qu¨¦ realizan las acciones, y comenten los resultados obtenidos; se espera mucho m¨¢s que unos bloques de c¨®digo.
La toma de decisiones sobre los datos se debe hacer considerando el contexto del problema y de los datos, no se puede ver todo solamente desde los ojos de los datos, sino tambi¨¦n considerar el negocio.
Un Cient¨ªfico de Datos debe poder comunicar los puntos importantes de su trabajo en un lenguaje universal para todos los p¨²blicos.
Todo esto se considerar¨¢ en la nota.
----------------------
# Evaluation

El taller ser¨¢ evaluado de esta manera: 

### Env¨ªos: 
Para la evaluaci¨®n se espera que: 
- env¨ªen un archivo con los resultados a Kaggle haciendo un submission 
- suban a Intu el notebook correspondiente teniendo en cuenta el contenido esperado detallado a continuaci¨®n 

### Entendimiento y preparaci¨®n de datos: 
- An¨¢lisis del baseline (0.2 puntos) 
- An¨¢lisis de missing values (0.2 puntos) 
- An¨¢lisis de outliers (0.2 puntos) 
- Imputaci¨®n de valores (0.4 puntos) 

### Feature Engineering: 
- Tratamiento de variables categ¨®ricas (0.2 puntos) 
- Uso de PCA (0.4 puntos)
- Selecci¨®n de variables (0.4 puntos) 

### Calibraci¨®n y selecci¨®n de modelo 
- Custom Transformers (0.4)
- Uso de Optimizaci¨®n bayesiana (0.6 puntos)
- SVC con diferentes kernels (0.8 puntos) 
- Redes neuronales densas poco profundas (1 punto) 
- Escogencia del flujo final (0.2 puntos) 

### Competencia 
Adicionalmente, al tratarse de una competencia, seg¨²n la posici¨®n en la misma se otorgar¨¢n puntos de bonificaci¨®n de la siguiente manera: 
- Primer grupo: 1 punto 
- Segundo grupo: 0.6 puntos 
- Tercer grupo: 0.3 puntos 

Para la competencia se tendr¨¢ en cuenta los resultados con la m¨¦trica de ROC AUC. A parte del dataset provisto a cada grupo, se tendr¨¢ un dataset de validaci¨®n no accesible directamente por los estudiantes, pero que se scorear¨¢ con cada submisi¨®n de resultados sobre un dataset privado.
Cada grupo deber¨¢ predecir la probabilidad de obtener un resultado de psa anormal como apoyo de detecci¨®n de cancer de prostata para instancia del test set, y se deber¨¢ subir un archivo a esta competencia de Kaggle con los resultados, ¨²nicamente dos columnas `ID` y `Target`, separadas por comas, tal como se muestra en el siguiente ejemplo: 

``` ID,Target 20012,0.551 1,0.326 ```","# Dataset Description

### Archivos
- train.parquet - El set de datos de entrenamiento
- test.parquet - El set de datos de test
- sample_submission.csv - un ejemplo de un archivo a someter en la competencia
- Diccionario.xslx - Descripci¨®n de los campos que se encuentran en el train y test set.

Para leer archivos parquet, seguir las instrucciones que encontrar¨¢n aqu¨ª (se pueden leer directamente a un pandas Dataframe, despu¨¦s de haber instalado el paquete fastparquet).
https://pandas.pydata.org/pandas-docs/version/0.21/io.html#io-parquet",False,True
8394,hawkins-ml-hunt,"# Overview

**Welcome to the Hawkins ML Hunt: An Epic Machine Learning Challenge!**

Step into the eerie, enigmatic town of Hawkins, where the boundary between reality and the supernatural is blurred. In this thrilling machine learning competition, you¡¯ll assume the role of a dedicated investigator on a mission to unearth the secrets of the Upside Down¡ªa parallel dimension filled with dark, mysterious forces.

### **The Mission**

Your objective is to delve into a unique and captivating dataset, representing the mysterious characters from the Upside Down. Each character possesses distinct supernatural abilities, weapons, and traits, which are intricately tied to their survival. As a participant, you are challenged to uncover the true essence of these characters by predicting their survival in various perilous situations.

### **The Challenge**

Participants will be provided with a dataset that includes a variety of features describing the enigmatic characters¡ªranging from their unique powers and weapons to their influence, agility, and more. The dataset also includes a crucial ""survival"" column, which indicates whether a character survived a particular scenario. This column will serve as the label for your training data.

Your task is to build robust predictive models that accurately forecast the survival probabilities of these characters. Can you decipher the code hidden within the data and predict which characters will survive the dangers of the Upside Down?
----------------------
# Description

### **What You¡¯ll Need to Do:**

1. **Analyze the Dataset:** 
   - Dive deep into the features provided, exploring the nuances of each character¡¯s traits, powers, and other significant attributes.
   - Leverage any supplementary information that may provide additional insights into character behavior and survivability.

2. **Build Predictive Models:** 
   - Utilize advanced machine learning techniques to develop models that can predict survival outcomes with high accuracy.
   - Experiment with different algorithms, feature engineering methods, and model evaluation techniques to optimize your predictions.

3. **Test and Iterate:** 
   - Validate your models against the test set, refine your approach based on the results, and iterate until you achieve the best possible performance.

### **The Ultimate Goal:**

To emerge as the top Hunter in this competition, your model must not only be precise but also innovative. The ability to interpret the subtle clues hidden within the dataset will be key to your success.

---

Good luck! We can¡¯t wait to see who will conquer the challenges of Hawkins and emerge victorious in this extraordinary ML hunt.
----------------------
# Evaluation

The evaluation metric for this competition is **Mean Absolute Error (MAE)**, measuring the average absolute difference between the predicted survivability and the actual survivability of Character in combat situations. Participants will compete against each other to develop the most accurate and reliable models, with the ultimate goal of uncovering invaluable insights that could potentially save lives on the battlefield.","# Dataset Description

**Welcome to The Hawkins ML Hunt !**

Prepare to delve into the eerie world of Hawkins, where you'll use your machine learning skills to predict the survival chances of enigmatic characters from the Upside Down.

**Files:**

- **train.csv:** This file contains the training set, filled with data on various attributes of supernatural beings, along with their mysterious survival outcomes.
- **test.csv:** This file includes the test set, where you'll apply your models to predict the survival probabilities of characters based on their unique features.
- **sample_submission.csv:** A sample submission file that demonstrates the correct format for submitting your predictions.

**Data Format:**
The data files are provided in CSV (Comma-Separated Values) format, a straightforward and accessible format compatible with various programming languages and data analysis tools.

Dive into the mystery, analyze the data, and reveal the secrets hidden in the shadows of Hawkins. Good luck, codebreaker!

Explore the dataset featuring:

- **Character_ID:** A unique identifier for each mysterious entity.
- **Character_Type:** The role or archetype of the character (e.g., ""Hero,"" ""Villain"").
- **Max_Power:** The maximum power level the character can achieve.
- **Weapon_Type:** The type of weapon or ability the character wields.
- **Influence_Range:** The extent of the character's influence.
- **Max_Awareness:** The maximum perception level of the character.
- **Energy_Source:** The type of supernatural energy the character uses.
- **Team_Size:** The number of allies or minions supporting the character.
- **Defense_Strength:** The level of defensive strength or armor.
- **Agility_Level:** The character's agility or flexibility.
- **Tech_Defense_Availability:** Technological defenses available for protection.
- **Surveillance_Capability:** The presence of surveillance or tracking systems.
- **Max_Environment_Adaptation:** The highest level of adaptation to different environments.
- **Power_Capacity:** The maximum energy capacity the character can hold.
- **Origin_Year:** The year the character emerged or was introduced.
- **Energy_Sources_Count:** The number of energy sources or powers utilized.
- **Energy_Reserve:** The amount of energy reserve maintained.
- **Escape_Maneuverability:** Ability to escape from perilous situations.
- **Vision_Scope:** The range or scope of the character¡¯s vision.
- **Max_Protection_Level:** The highest protection or shielding level available.
- **Operational_Influence_with_Max_Resources:** Influence when using maximum resources.
- **Core_Material:** The core essence or material of the character.
- **Burden_Capacity:** The capacity the character can manage.
- **Escape_Speed:** The speed of escape or retreat.
- **Landing_Speed:** The speed required for safe landing after intense scenarios.
- **Perception_Clarity:** The clarity of perception in intense situations.

Dive into the unknown, harness your machine learning skills, and help us uncover the secrets of Hawkins. Are you ready to reveal the hidden truths? Join the Codebreaker Challenge today!

**Prediction:**
Participants are challenged to forecast the survival of these enigmatic characters based on the provided features. The survival column in the training set contains the labels needed to train your predictive models. Your objective is to build precise and effective models that can anticipate the survival probabilities of these characters in various perilous scenarios.

We encourage you to dive deep into the dataset, utilize the supplementary information provided, and employ innovative machine learning techniques to uncover crucial insights into character survivability. Best of luck, and may the most skilled codebreakers emerge victorious in this thrilling challenge!",False,True
