8404,fit-5215-object-detection-s-2-2024,"# Description

This is the home page of the competition. This competition is organized for the FIT5215: Deep Learning unit at Monash University. The students who are interested can join in this competition.

The students can use any techniques in machine learning and deep learning in this competition. This is an individual competition and your team name must contain your student ID to facilitate us in marking.

Hope that you enjoy this competition. Have funs!!
----------------------
# Evaluation

<p></p><h2>Evaluation Metric</h2>
<p>The evaluation metric for this competition is the accuracy </p><p>
</p><h2>Submission Format</h2>
<p><strong>Please follow the file my_solution.csv in the tab Data to submit your result.</strong></p>","# Dataset Description

This page contains the datasets and their information for the FIT5215 object classification competition. There are three zip and one CSV file as follows:

- **train_dataset**: the labeled training set with 10,000 images and 20 classes.

- **test_dataset**: the unlabeled testing dataset of images of the size (64, 64, 3).

- **my_solution.csv**: the template for a submitted file.",False,True
8405,mma-865,"# Overview

In this competition, participants are tasked with predicting the success of loan applications submitted by the business based on various economical and demographical features. The goal is to build a model that can accurately determine whether the business would be able to return the loan amount or not. This model will aid microfinance institutions in decision-making processes and optimize their impact on underprivileged communities worldwide.
----------------------
# Description

Microfinance has emerged as a pivotal economic force, offering financial services to underserved populations. This competition provides datasets containing loan applications from various countries. Each entry includes the applicant's gender, loan amount, country, sector, and more. Participants will use this data to predict which loans are likely to be repaid. 

This would be a binary classification problem, where 'status' would be the target variable with two classes :
0 - if the loan would not be repaid
1 - if the loan would be repaid 


----------------------
# Evaluation

The metric that would be used for evaluation is ROC AUC. The sample submission should be a CSV file, only containing two columns - id and status. The values in status columns should be probability of positive class (i.e. class = 1).

Below is a sample...

id, status
545, 0
546, 1
547, 1
----------------------
# Submission

Please click on Team tab and enter your team name there. For example: ""Team Dundas"". All submissions must be made with valid team name only.","# Dataset Description

kiva_train.csv: This training dataset includes entries with variables such as country, business description (en), gender, loan amount, nonpayment type, sector, and the loan status (1 for repaid, 0 for default).

kiva_test.csv: The testing set, used for predictions, mirrors the training set structure but omits the 'status' column, including over 1,300 entries.",False,True
