8430,first-steps-in-data-science-new,"# Overview

First Steps in Data Science  competition is designed specifically for beginners in the field of Machine Learning (ML), making it a perfect opportunity for anyone interested in exploring this exciting domain.
----------------------
# Description

The competition is aimed at introducing participants to the basics of Machine Learning and the Kaggle platform. It provides an opportunity to apply ML techniques to solve real-world problems, even if you have no prior experience in the field.
**Task: Regression**
The task is to predict the values of the ""Target"" column using machine learning algorithms.
----------------------
# Evaluation

The evaluation metric for this competition is the Root Mean Squared Error (RMSE).

RMSE is a commonly used metric for evaluating the accuracy of a regression model. It measures the average difference between the predicted values and the actual values. The lower the RMSE, the better the model is at predicting the actual values.

https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Root-mean-square_deviation
