8439,pmu-cai-competition2024,"# Overview

Center for Artificial Intelligence (CAI) at Prince Mohammad Bin Fahd University is challenging all developers to build an algorithm that automatically detects objects live. 

The submitted algorithm must detect many things in the video and show bounding boxes with annotation. Computers are getting better at vision, however, in a few critical scenarios, they cannot match human perception. 

To make it challenging, instead of static photos, let¡¯s make it dynamic where things change based on the scene. CAI wants to push the capabilities of computer vision and AI.

In case you are facing issues submitting your final project, you can email us at: cai@pmu.edu.sa 
----------------------
# Description

Design and train an AI model using the provided training dataset featuring various objects. The competition will involve running your trained model on a separate, unseen testing video dataset that will be provided later. The winning model will be the one that achieves the highest combined score based on a weighted metric that factors in all three criteria.
----------------------
# Evaluation

Submissions are subjected to be tested on a testing video that CAI provides, and then evaluated by computing a weighted metric that factors in all three criteria.

**1- Speed:** How quickly can your model identify and localize objects within a live video stream? Measured in milliseconds (ms).

**2- Accuracy:** How precisely can your model distinguish and classify objects? 

**3- Memory:** How efficiently does your model utilize computing resources? Measured in megabytes (MB).

A weighted score will be calculated based on the three metrics mentioned above. The competition committee will determine the specific weights depending on the competition's focus. The model with the highest weighted score will be crowned the champion

----------------------
# Prize

The winners will be awarded prizes and receive recognition. 

First Best Model: **15,000 SAR**
Second Best Model: **10,000 SAR**
Third Best Model in Saudi: **5,000 SAR**","# Dataset Description

**Overview**

The provided dataset is a subset of the well-known ImageNet image database, focusing on a specific set of 57 object categories. This dataset maintains the high-quality image and annotation standards of its parent dataset while providing a more focused collection for a specific challenge.

**Content**

**1- Images:** A collection of digital images depicting 57 distinct object categories.
**2- Annotations:** Detailed metadata associated with each image, including:
        - Object bounding boxes: Precisely defined rectangular regions enclosing the objects of interest.
        - Object class labels: Categorical designations corresponding to the 57 object classes.
**3- Testing Videos:** All testing videos can be downloaded from the following link (https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1OUr-edxMZkR1-j7NEDwJ36Ye_GCKmxoc?usp=sharing).
**Source Dataset**

The provided dataset is derived from the ImageNet dataset, inheriting its rigorous data collection and annotation processes.

**Purpose**

This dataset is designed to launch a challenge in computer vision tasks such as object detection and localization, specifically within the context of the 57 defined object categories.",False,True
