# Evaluation

The following is the Evaluation techniue for the main competition, though same submission format & evaliation technique is also applicable for test Loan competition.

In this AI-Powered Drug Repurposing competition, participants will build machine learning models to predict drug-protein interactions. The evaluation process will be based on the following key metrics:

AUC-ROC (Area Under the ROC Curve):
This will measure the model's ability to distinguish between positive (interaction) and negative (no interaction) cases across different thresholds.
A higher AUC value (closer to 1) indicates better model performance in identifying drug-protein interactions.

Submission Format:
Participants are expected to submit their predictions as a CSV file.
The file must include two columns:
ID: The unique identifier for each sample.
Prediction: The predicted probability or binary classification (0 or 1) for drug-protein interaction.

Example Submission:
ID	Prediction
1	0.85
2	0.10
3	0.75
4	0.05
5	0.60

The final leaderboard will be determined based on the performance of models on a hidden test set, with the focus on AUC-ROC.","# Dataset Description

