8550,k-2-praktikum-ii-nb-dtl-random-forest-xg-boost,"# Overview

Mahasiswa mengimplementasikan beberapa algoritma machine learning untuk klasifikasi antara lain Decision Tree, Bayesian Network, Random Forest, dan XGBoost. Algoritma diimplementasikan menggunakan bahasa pemrograman Python dengan bantuan library scikit-learn untuk menangani kasus yang ditentukan.
----------------------
# Description

Capaian Praktikum:
Diharapkan mahasiswa dapat mengerti dasar dalam metode pengolahan data untuk membangun model Decision Tree, Bayesian Network, Random Forest, dan XGBoost serta cara menganalisa kekurangan dan kelebihan dari model yang sudah dibangun.

Persiapan Praktikum:
Berikut adalah beberapa hal yang harus disiapkan oleh mahasiswa agar dapat melaksanakan praktikum:

- Laptop atau PC
- Koneksi internet
- Akun Kaggle
- IDE seperti Jupyter Notebook, Google Colab, dan sebagainya
----------------------
# Evaluation

Akurasi adalah salah satu metrik kinerja yang paling umum digunakan karena mudah dipahami dan dihitung. Namun, penting untuk diingat bahwa akurasi tidak selalu menjadi metrik yang paling relevan untuk semua kasus. Untuk menghitung akurasi, kita perlu membandingkan prediksi model dengan nilai aktual.

**Akurasi = (Jumlah prediksi benar) / (Jumlah total prediksi)**


## Submission File
Untuk setiap ID dalam data pengujian, anda harus memprediksi probabilitas untuk variabel TARGET. File harus berisi header dan memiliki format berikut:

    ID,TARGET
    2,0
    5,0
    6,0
    etc.","# Dataset Description

Sebuah **transformator dapat mengalami kegagalan** karena berbagai alasan, tetapi penyebab yang paling umum termasuk sambaran petir, kelebihan beban, keausan dan korosi, lonjakan daya, dan kelembapan. Terlepas dari penyebabnya, hasilnya bisa sangat dramatis. Transformator mengandung minyak mineral untuk menjaga transformator tetap dingin. Ketika transformator kelebihan beban, kabelnya dapat menghasilkan panas dan percikan api. Tekanan berlebih yang besar ini dapat menyebabkan transformator meledak dengan suara keras, kilatan cahaya, dan bahkan bola api yang dapat menghasilkan gumpalan asap besar yang dapat dilihat dari jarak jauh.

**Cited :**
Arias Vel¨¢squez, Ricardo Manuel; Mejia Lara, Jennifer (2020), ¡°Data for: Root cause analysis improved with machine learning for failure analysis in power transformers¡±, Mendeley Data, V1, doi: 10.17632/rz75w3fkxy.1",False,True
8551,predicting-subscription-to-a-streaming-service,"# Overview

Competition Overview
Welcome to the Streaming Service Subscription Prediction Challenge!

In this competition, your task is to build a machine learning model that predicts whether users will subscribe to a fictional streaming service based on a variety of features related to their demographics and behavior.

Goal:
Your objective is to create a model that accurately predicts user subscriptions using the provided training dataset. You will be evaluated based on your model's performance on the unseen test set. The dataset includes a variety of features, such as age, gender, subscription type, and user engagement metrics, making it essential to explore and analyze the data to uncover patterns that influence subscription decisions.

Key Features:
Data-Driven Insights: Leverage user data to enhance marketing strategies and improve customer retention.
Imbalanced Dataset: The challenge includes a highly imbalanced target variable, requiring you to apply techniques to handle class imbalance effectively.
Engage with the Community: Collaborate and learn from fellow data scientists and machine learning enthusiasts as you refine your approach.
Get Started:
Download the datasets from the ""Data"" tab.
Familiarize yourself with the evaluation criteria.
Submit your predictions in the specified format.
Join us in this exciting competition and showcase your skills in predictive modeling! Good luck!


----------------------
# Description

Background: In today¡¯s digital age, streaming services have become a popular form of entertainment. To optimize marketing strategies and enhance customer retention, it¡¯s crucial for companies to predict whether users will subscribe to a service based on various features related to their behavior and demographics.

Dataset Overview: You are provided with a synthetic dataset representing potential customers for a streaming service. The dataset contains various features that may influence a user's decision to subscribe to a service, along with the target variable indicating whether the user subscribed or not.

Files:

train.csv - The training set
test.csv - The test set
sample_submission.csv - A sample submission file in the correct format
----------------------
# Evaluation

The evaluation section describes how submissions will be scored and how participants should format their submissions. You don't need a sub-title at the top; the page title appears above. Below is an example of a typical evaluation page.

---

Submissions are evaluated on [area under the ROC curve](http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Receiver_operating_characteristic) between the predicted probability and the observed target.


## Submission File
For each ID in the test set, you must predict a probability for the TARGET variable. The file should contain a header and have the following format:

    ID,target
    2,yes
    5,no
    6,yes
    etc.","# Dataset Description

Files:

train.csv - The training set
test.csv - The test set
sample_submission.csv - A sample submission file in the correct format
Input Variables:

user_id: Unique identifier for each user.
age (numeric): Age of the user.
gender (categorical): Gender of the user (e.g., ""male"", ""female"").
subscription_type (categorical): Type of subscription (e.g., ""basic"", ""premium"", ""family"").
monthly_income (numeric): User's monthly income in USD.
num_devices (numeric): Number of devices connected to the service.
watching_hours (numeric): Average hours spent watching content per week.
last_payment_date (date): Date of the last payment made by the user.
has_trial (binary): Indicates whether the user had a free trial (e.g., ""yes"", ""no"").
feedback_score (numeric): User's feedback score ranging from 1 to 5.
country (categorical): Country of residence of the user.
preferred_genre (categorical): User's preferred genre of content (e.g., ""action"", ""drama"", ""comedy"").
promo_code_used (binary): Indicates whether a promotional code was used (e.g., ""yes"", ""no"").
watching_frequency (categorical): Frequency of watching (e.g., ""daily"", ""weekly"", ""monthly"").
last_contact_date (date): Date of the last contact with the user by the service team.
Output Variable (Target): 16. target (binary): Indicates whether the user subscribed to the streaming service (e.g., ""yes"", ""no"").",False,True
8552,competenciapruebaacmcusco,"# Overview

Esta es una replica de una de las competencias de Kaggle m¨¢s famosas que existen, el objetivo de esta es probar las funcionalidades y que tanto los competidores como los organizadores se familiarizen con la plataforma.

Objetivo: Probar las funcionalidades de Kaggle.
----------------------
# Description


El hundimiento del Titanic es uno de los naufragios m¨¢s infames de la historia.

El 15 de abril de 1912, durante su viaje inaugural, el ampliamente considerado ""insumergible"" RMS Titanic se hundi¨® tras chocar con un iceberg. Desafortunadamente, no hab¨ªa suficientes botes salvavidas para todos a bordo, lo que result¨® en la muerte de 1502 de los 2224 pasajeros y tripulantes.

Si bien hubo un elemento de suerte involucrado en la supervivencia, parece que algunos grupos de personas ten¨ªan m¨¢s probabilidades de sobrevivir que otros.

En este desaf¨ªo, te pedimos que construyas un modelo predictivo que responda a la pregunta: ""?qu¨¦ tipo de personas ten¨ªan m¨¢s probabilidades de sobrevivir?"" utilizando datos de los pasajeros (es decir, nombre, edad, g¨¦nero, clase socioecon¨®mica, etc.).
----------------------
# Evaluation

Objetivo
Tu tarea es predecir si un pasajero sobrevivi¨® al hundimiento del Titanic o no. Para cada pasajero en el conjunto de prueba, debes predecir un valor de 0 o 1 para la variable.

M¨¦trica
Tu puntaje ser¨¢ el porcentaje de pasajeros que predices correctamente. Esto se conoce como precisi¨®n (accuracy).

Formato del archivo de env¨ªo
Debes enviar un archivo CSV con exactamente 418 registros m¨¢s una fila de encabezado. Tu env¨ªo mostrar¨¢ un error si tienes columnas adicionales (m¨¢s all¨¢ de PassengerId y Survived) o filas.
El archivo debe tener exactamente 2 columnas:

- **PassengerId** (ordenado en cualquier orden)
- **Survived** (contiene tus predicciones binarias: 1 para sobrevivi¨®, 0 para falleci¨®)

### Ejemplo de formato:

PassengerId,Survived
