Considering the inherent randomness of large language models (LLMs) and the importance of maintaining transparency in the competition, we have decided to exclude this task to ensure fair and consistent evaluation for all participants. Therefore, task 2 [Generation] is not part of this challenge and will not be evaluated. The primary objective of Task 1 is to maximize retrieval accuracy, ensuring that the system identifies the most relevant and correct contexts from the financial datasets provided.
----------------------
# Evaluation

# Task 1 [Retrieval]
For the **Task 1**, evaluation of retrieval process will use the **NDCG@10 (Normalized Discounted Cumulative Gain)** metric. NDCG is a commonly used metric in information retrieval to evaluate the ranking quality of search results. It measures how well the predicted ranking of relevant documents matches the ideal ranking. NDCG@10 specifically evaluates the top 10 results returned for each query. 

We recommend using the **GitHub repository** [FinanceRAG](https://github.com/linq-rag/FinanceRAG) to run simple baseline code or streamline development for the challenge.

``` shell
git clone https://github.com/linq-rag/FinanceRAG.git
```

## Submission File

For every **query_id** in the test set, you are required to predict the probability of the **TARGET context** in the corpus. The submission file should contain two columns: **query_id** and **corpus_id**.

Each **query_id** should be associated with the top 10 **corpus_id** predictions, ordered by probability, with the most probable context listed first.

The submission file must include a header and follow this format:

```
query_id, corpus_id
```

You are required to **submit a single `CSV` file** that consolidates the results from all datasets.

    query_id,corpus_id
    qd496c6a0,dd4b92b32
    qd496c6a0,dd4ba2a5a
    qd496c6a0,dd4be1f98
    ...
    qd496c9c0,dd4b9f292
    qd496c9c0,dd4c5d6ca
    qd496c9c0,dd4b9ec5c
    etc..

As a baseline solution for participating in the competition, please refer to [this Kaggle notebook](https://www.kaggle.com/code/jihoonkwon/baseline-with-official-github-repository). This notebook demonstrates an example of implementing Retrieval and Reranking for the FinDER Task using the SentenceTransformers package.

*Note*: To submit to the competition, you must save the results for all tasks and combine them into a single file.

