8640,predict-app-users-next-step-release-version,"# Overview

Modern mobile applications have become an indispensable part of people's daily lives. Whether it's shopping, ordering food, traveling, or socializing and entertainment, people increasingly rely on mobile apps to meet various needs. In this context, understanding user behavior patterns and predicting their next actions are crucial for improving user experience, optimizing product design, and enhancing business value.

The goal of this data competition is to build a model to predict users' next actions in the app based on their historical operation records. The competition dataset contains a large amount of real application usage logs, recording the operation trajectories of numerous users across different times and functional modules. Participants need to utilize this data, extract valuable features, select appropriate algorithmic models, and ultimately provide predictions for each user's next action under specific states.

Accurately predicting user behavior will bring tremendous value to mobile applications in areas such as personalized recommendations, process optimization, and advertising placement. This competition topic is closely aligned with real business application scenarios and has strong practical significance. We warmly welcome data scientists, algorithm engineers, and related professionals from all sectors to actively participate, demonstrate your expertise, and jointly explore the latest theories and practical methods in the frontier field of behavior prediction.

