8642,air-traffic-prediction,"# Overview


This dataset provides monthly operational metrics for a major Indian airline from 2013. It includes information on the number of departures, flight hours, distance flown, passenger traffic, available seat kilometers, freight carried, and mail carried. This dataset is valuable for analyzing the airline's performance, identifying trends and predicting future demand.

Time Period: Monthly Data from 2013

**Goal:** Predicting passenger demand for the next 12 months.
----------------------
# Description

You can use any popular time series library for this task. (sktime, u8darts, GluonTS, etc..) 
You need to predict 'PASSENGERS CARRIED' from 2023 Sep to 2024 Aug.
Do the necessary Feature Engineering/Data Cleanup required to create time-series in your choice of library. 

Part(a): Only Models discussed in class or its variant are allowed for submission for the competition.
Part(b): Use an LLM to generate predictions. Report your best working prompting strategy see sec 3 [LLMS as zero shot predictors] (https://arxiv.org/abs/2310.07820) for some ideas on tokenisation of input, handling null values. Report evaluations on your validation set for its predictions in the report. DO NOT submit predictions from LLM here.
Part(c) Train a Global Model (Fit once on related time series and used later for prediction instead of fitted for every time series separately) to predict. You can use any of the other columns present in the dataset to create related Time-series. Again Only report evaluations by this method in the report.

To be included in the report: 
- how were hyperparameters(p,d,q, seasonality order, etc) chosen.
- Outlier smoothing/ missing value imputation strategy.
- how was train/val performed and best model chosen (eval on validation)
- part(b), part(c)
----------------------
# Evaluation

---

Submissions are evaluated on MAPE on the holdout Test Data.
https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mean_absolute_percentage_error
Keep your Roll no as your Kaggle account name before submission.
## Submission File
The file should contain a header and have the following format:
See Sample Submission for more details.
   YEAR_MONTH, PASSENGERS CARRIED
    ""2023 SEP"", 234790
   .. etc","# Dataset Description

## Files

*   **AirtrafficA4.csv** - historical data

*   **sample_submission.csv** - a sample submission file in the correct format


* **parkingLot.csv** - Dataset for Q1 in the Assignment

## Columns

 Name	Description		
* AIRLINE - Name of the airline 		
* YEAR -	Year of the data (2013)		
* MONTH - Month of the data (e.g., ""Jan"", ""Feb"")		
* TOTAL DEPARTURES - Total number of departures for the month (Be careful number in comma sep string format e.g ""00,00,000"") 	
* HOURS FLOWN	- Total number of hours flown by the airline's aircraft (Be careful number in comma sep string format e.g ""00,00,000"") 	
* KILOMETRE FLOWN	- Total distance flown by the airline's aircraft (in kilometers)		
* PASSENGERS CARRIED	- Total number of passengers carried by the airline(Be careful number in comma sep string format e.g ""00,00,000"") 	
* AVAILABLE SEAT KILOMETRE (IN THOUSAND)- Total available seat kilometers (ASKs) offered by the airline (in thousands)		
* FREIGHT CARRIED (IN TONNE) - 	Total freight carried by the airline (in tonnes)		
* MAIL CARRIED (IN TONNE)- Total mail carried by the airline (in tonnes)",False,True
