8646,asrm-455,"# Overview

This is the individual project/in-class Kaggle competition of ASRM 455  Predictive
Analytics Fall 2024 
----------------------
# Description

This is a open project on data analytics. You are expected to perform data analysis, preprocessing, model selection, feature selection, ¡­ based on the prediction task.

You may consult resources like textbooks and Internet materials. You may use any analytics software to complete the analysis as instructed. However, you may not discuss the specific business problem, data, or tasks with others.
----------------------
# Evaluation

1. Grading and Submission Details:
This document and the report template indicate the points assigned to each of the components, totaling 100 points. Grading criteria include:
? Quality of thought process
? Code
? Conclusions and clarity in the report
When instructed, include specific output (tables or graphs) in your response. These are required at minimum, but displaying additional relevant output is encouraged.

2. Submission Requirements in Canvas
At a minimum, submit:
? A completed report template (Word, .docx) containing your task responses.
? An .Rmd file that supports your analysis. This file should run from start to finish and clearly indicate.Your thought process and conclusions for each task must be fully contained within your Word report. The. Rmd file should be clear, may contain comments, and should directly support the analysis provided in your report.

3. For Kaggle Submission:
Your submission file should be a CSV with the following structure:

ID: This should be the numbers 1 to 4, each corresponding to a specific metric.
Value: This should contain the values for the following metrics, in this order:
- AUC_Train_classification
- AUC_Test_classification
- Pearson goodness-of-fit statistic on training data
- Pearson goodness-of-fit statistic on testing data
Make sure your file format and column names exactly match the competition specifications to avoid errors during scoring.","# Dataset Description

Data Dictionary Summary

**days**: Number of days between hospital admission and discharge.
Type: Integer (1-14)

**gender**: Patient¡¯s gender.
Values: Female, Male

**age**: Age of the patient grouped in ten-year intervals.
Values: [0, 10), [10, 20), ¡­, [90, 100)

**race**: Patient¡¯s race/ethnicity.
Values: AfricanAmerican, Asian, Caucasian, Hispanic, Other

**weight**: Patient¡¯s weight, categorized in twenty-five-pound intervals.
Values: [0, 25), [25, 50), ¡­, [175, 200)

**admit_type_id**: Type of hospital admission.
Values:
1 = Emergency
2 = Urgent
3 = Elective
4 = Not Available

**metformin**: Indicates whether metformin was prescribed or if there was a change in dosage upon admission.
Values:
Up = dosage increased
Down = dosage decreased
Steady = no change in dosage
No = not prescribed

**insulin**: Indicates whether insulin was prescribed or if there was a change in dosage upon admission.
Values:
Up = dosage increased
Down = dosage decreased
Steady = no change in dosage
No = not prescribed

**readmitted**: Indicates whether the patient had been readmitted within 12 months prior to the encounter.
Values:
No  = no record of readmission
**<**=readmitted in less than 30 days
**>**= readmitted in more than 30 days  


**num_procs**:Number of procedures performed in the 12 months prior to the encounter.
Type: Integer (0-6)

**num_meds**:Number of distinct medications administered in the 12 months prior to the encounter.
Type: Integer (1-67)

**num_ip**: Number of inpatient visits in the 12 months prior to the encounter.
Type: Integer (0-21)

**num_diags**:Number of diagnoses entered into the system in the 12 months prior to the encounter.
Type: Integer (1-16)",False,True
8647,af-ii-2024-ii-object-localization,"# Description

Se requiere desarrollar un modelo predictivo que tiene que determinar la clasificaci¨®n y localizaci¨®n de  Pinguinos o Tortugas que aparecen en una imagen. Se le proporciona un conjunto de datos que contiene im¨¢genes y sus anotaciones correspondientes. Su modelo debe detectar qu¨¦ animal es y la ubicaci¨®n en la foto.
----------------------
# Evaluation


- **CNN personalizado:** 

Cree un modelo de red neuronal convolucional personalizado como backbone (features extractor) y entr¨¦nelo desde cero (1,5 puntos) 

- **Predicci¨®n del cuadro delimitador (Bounding box):** 

Implemente una cabeza de regresi¨®n que se alimenta con las caracter¨ªsticas extra¨ªdas del backbone convolucional. (1 punto) 

- **Clasificaci¨®n de objetos:** 

Implementar una cabeza de clasificaci¨®n que se alimenta con las caracter¨ªsticas extra¨ªdas del backbone convolucional (1 punto) 

- **Aumento de datos (Data Augmentation):** 

Compara el uso de diferentes t¨¦cnicas de aumento de datos para ver su impacto en el desempe?o de ambas tareas (clasificaci¨®n y regresi¨®n) (0,5 puntos) 

- **Transferir aprendizaje (Transfer learning):** 

Usar dos modelos preentrenados como backbones y conectar los creados previamente cabezas de clasificaci¨®n y regresi¨®n para recibir entradas de ellas. (1 punto) 


- **Competencia** 

Adicionalmente, al tratarse de una competencia, seg¨²n la posici¨®n en la misma se otorgar¨¢n puntos de bonificaci¨®n de la siguiente manera: 

* Primer grupo: 1 punto 
* Segundo grupo: 0.6 puntos 
* Tercer grupo: 0.3 puntos 

Tengan en cuenta que deben seguir un protocolo correcto de evaluaci¨®n para evitar la fuga de datos de los conjuntos de prueba en los pasos de procesamiento de datos. Los errores ser¨¢n sancionados (-0,5 puntos cada uno). La m¨¦trica de evaluaci¨®n para esta competencia es el [coeficiente de dados] (https://www.kaggle.com/code/yerramvarun/understanding-dice-coefficient/notebook) para la tarea de regresi¨®n de cuadro delimitador y [accuracy](https://developers.google.com/machine-learning/crash-course/classification/accuracy) para la tarea de clasificaci¨®n de objetos. 

## Submission 

**Para cada conjunto de t¨¦cnicas en el dataset**, los submission deben contener las siguientes columnas: 

    filename,class_id
    image_id_000_.jpg,1
    image_id_001_.jpg,2
    image_id_002_.jpg,2
    etc.","# Dataset Description

## Files

*   **train.csv** - the training set
*   **test.csv** - the test set
*   **sample_submission.csv** - a sample submission file in the correct format
*  **images.zip** - images folder",False,True
