## Dataset Files and Directories

- `train/` folder contains 30,000 images that are labelled in `train_metadata.csv` 
- `test/` contains 10,000 images which are not labelled externally; for this ""label"" is what you have to predict.
- `LICENSE.txt` cites the use of the [captcha Python Library](https://github.com/lepture/captcha/blob/master/) while making the dataset - both train and test sets.


## train_metadata.csv

- `image_name`: The name of the image (extension included), such as `0.png`, `1.png`, ... , `n.png` where n is a positive natural number.

- `captcha_text`: The text that the image holds in the form of captcha. It is the actual value which is present in the image. **This is your target variable for the submission**",False,True
