8792,copia-competencia-para-estudiar,"# Description

Los bancos, y en general los establecimientos de cr¨¦dito, necesitan captar recursos para financiar sus operaciones y actividades. Una forma com¨²n en la que los bancos obtienen fondos es a trav¨¦s de la emisi¨®n de certificados de dep¨®sito a t¨¦rmino (CDT). 

Los bancos utilizan los fondos captados de los CDT para conceder pr¨¦stamos a empresas y particulares, para invertir en activos financieros o para cumplir con los requisitos de reserva que exigen los reguladores. Por estos motivos, poder predecir si un cliente va a adquirir uno de estos productos es un problema de negocio muy relevante que debe resolver un banco.

El objetivo de este taller es que de acuerdo a la base de datos de campa?as de mercadeo que se realiz¨® con los clientes de un banco, puedan predecir si ese cliente adquiri¨® o no adquiri¨® un CDT. 

----------------------
# Evaluation

M¨¦trica de evaluaci¨®n: **Accuracy**

La m¨¦trica de accuracy es una medida com¨²nmente utilizada en problemas de clasificaci¨®n para evaluar el rendimiento de un modelo y va a ser la utilizada para evaluar el desempe?o de cada uno de sus modelos. Se define como la proporci¨®n de predicciones correctas realizadas por el modelo en relaci¨®n con el n¨²mero total de predicciones. Matem¨¢ticamente, se expresa de la siguiente manera:

El accuracy proporciona una visi¨®n general de la capacidad del modelo para predecir correctamente las clases de los datos. Cuanto mayor sea el valor de la m¨¦trica, mejor ser¨¢ el rendimiento del modelo en t¨¦rminos de hacer predicciones precisas.

Sin embargo, es importante tener en cuenta que el accuracy puede no ser la m¨¦trica m¨¢s adecuada en todos los casos, especialmente cuando los datos est¨¢n desequilibrados.


Para subir sus predicciones a esta competencia, el archivo deber¨¢ tener el siguiente formato:

- Debe ser un archivo csv
- Debe tener 2 columnas llamadas: id, target","# Dataset Description

##**Archivos**

*   **train.csv** - El dataset de entrenamiento
*   **pred.csv** - El dataset que deben predecir
*   **ejemplo_predicciones.csv** - Un ejemplo del formato que deben tener los archivos de predicciones para ingresarlos a Kaggle

## **Columnas**

age (numeric)
job : type of job (categorical: ""admin."",""blue-collar"",""entrepreneur"",""housemaid"",""management"",""retired"",""self-employed"",""services"",""student"",""technician"",""unemployed"",""unknown"")
marital : marital status (categorical: ""divorced"",""married"",""single"",""unknown""; note: ""divorced"" means divorced or widowed)
  education (categorical: ""basic.4y"",""basic.6y"",""basic.9y"",""high.school"",""illiterate"",""professional.course"",""university.degree"",""unknown"")
default: has credit in default? (categorical: ""no"",""yes"",""unknown"")
  housing: has housing loan? (categorical: ""no"",""yes"",""unknown"")
loan: has personal loan? (categorical: ""no"",""yes"",""unknown"")
   # related with the last contact of the current campaign:
 contact: contact communication type (categorical: ""cellular"",""telephone"") 
month: last contact month of year (categorical: ""jan"", ""feb"", ""mar"", ..., ""nov"", ""dec"")
day_of_week: last contact day of the week (categorical: ""mon"",""tue"",""wed"",""thu"",""fri"")

   # other attributes:
campaign: number of contacts performed during this campaign and for this client (numeric, includes last contact)
pdays: number of days that passed by after the client was last contacted from a previous campaign (numeric; 999 means client was not previously contacted)
previous: number of contacts performed before this campaign and for this client (numeric)
poutcome: outcome of the previous marketing campaign (categorical: ""failure"",""nonexistent"",""success"")
   # social and economic context attributes
emp.var.rate: employment variation rate - quarterly indicator (numeric)
cons.price.idx: consumer price index - monthly indicator (numeric)     
cons.conf.idx: consumer confidence index - monthly indicator (numeric)     
nr.employed: number of employees - quarterly indicator (numeric)",False,True
8793,decision-trees-from-scratch-2024,"# Description

In this competition, you will predict whether or not someone has a cardiovascular disease given info about their health. You can use either a decision tree or a random forest.

Don't use any libraries like scikit learn. You should code the decision tree algorithm yourself. You can use numpy and pandas for simple computation and data IO if you wish. However, it is entirely possible to do this competition without any libraries.

You can find shell code in slideshow for the random forests lecture at https://tjmachinelearning.com/schedule/2324

For some more decision trees resources, check out a learning resources guide we compiled for the 2020 National Machine Learning Open competition we hosted (https://docs.google.com/document/d/1VoxJVC6Vv13XN2XuJFd5ZMcaCBCCJnjYHvQaxpjfuRE/edit?usp=sharing)

As always, if you are still confused on how to get started there are lots of great decision tree tutorials out there (for example https://machinelearningmastery.com/implement-decision-tree-algorithm-scratch-python/), and you can always reach out to any of the officers or email tjmachinelearning@gmail.com for help
----------------------
# Evaluation

We will be using categorization accuracy to score submissions (percentage of correct classifications)","# Dataset Description

<h1>Data</h1>
_________________________
<strong>The features you will receive are:</strong>

age (in number of days)

gender (1 for women, 2 for men)

height (in cm)

weight (in kg)

aphi (systolic blood pressure)

aplo (diastolic blood pressure)

cholesterol (1 for normal, 2 for above normal, 3 for well above normal)

gluc (glucose levels, 1 for normal, 2 for above normal, 3 for well above normal)

smoke (whether or not the individual smokes)

alco (whether or not the person consumes alcohol, 0 or 1)

active (whether person engages in some form of physical activity)

_________________________________

<strong>The target (what you will be trying to predict):</strong>

cardio (whether or not the individual has a cardiovascular disease)

_____________________________
<h2>File descriptions</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>train.csv</strong> - the training set</li>
<li><strong>test.csv</strong> - the test set</li>
<li><strong>sample.csv</strong> - a sample submission file in the correct format</li>
</ul>",False,True
