# Evaluation

Submissions are evaluated on the Root Mean Squared Prediction Error.

## Submission File
For each ID in the test set, you must predict a value for the **medv** variable. The file should contain a header and have the following format:

   id, medv
388,23.16111133
389,22.52786134
390,7.62076425
391,15.53813486

    etc.
----------------------
# Submission requirements

Requirement

The goal of the project is on getting better prediction on the median value of owner-occupied homes in $1000's. You are required to build three predictive models. Options of the predictive models include first-order linear regression models and polynomial models). Note that you cannot use the same class of model with different parameters. That is, the three fitted models you propose should be different in nature. For each of the models, you should have a score after submitting your prediction on Kaggle. To submit, hit the submission tab, and upload a csv file in the required format. In the end of your report, you should include a table summarizing these scores, as well as taking a screenshot of your best performance. You also need to attach on Crowdmark your submission files to Kaggle for verification.

Your report should contain the following components in a structured way.
* A brief introduction (goal, data, background)
* Exploratory data analysis and discussions (summary statistics, graphical analysis)
* Descriptions and discussions on the proposed three predictive models
* Your prediction scores on Kaggle

To help you get started, I provide a file on OnQ for constructing a regression model, and generating the submission file to Kaggle in the required format.

More information
* Due: 11:59 PM EST,  Dec 9 on Crowdmark.
* Your grade will be based on the quality of your report, effort, and most importantly the performance of your prediction rules. Your submission on Crowdmark should include: (1) A report, with no more than 10 pages. Be descriptive and concise. See the above Requirement section for details; (2) All your code files; (3) Three submission files to Kaggle in the required format. You should of course include those files with your best performance. Note that all the files to Crowdmark must be in PDF, JPG or PNG form.
* You will need to create a Kaggle account to be able to make submissions. For privacy, you do NOT need to use your name as the user name (any user name will do).
* You can only have two submissions per day","# Dataset Description

The following describes the dataset columns:

    CRIM - per capita crime rate by town
    ZN - proportion of residential land zoned for lots over 25,000 sq.ft.
    INDUS - proportion of non-retail business acres per town.
    CHAS - Charles River dummy variable (1 if tract bounds river; 0 otherwise)
    NOX - nitric oxides concentration (parts per 10 million)
    RM - average number of rooms per dwelling
    AGE - proportion of owner-occupied units built prior to 1940
    DIS - weighted distances to five Boston employment centres
    RAD - index of accessibility to radial highways
    TAX - full-value property-tax rate per $10,000
    PTRATIO - pupil-teacher ratio by town
    B - 1000(Bk - 0.63)^2 where Bk is the proportion of blacks by town
    LSTAT - % lower status of the population
    MEDV - Median value of owner-occupied homes in $1000's


## Files

*   **train.csv** - the training set
*   **test.csv** - the test set
*   **sample_submission.csv** - a sample submission file in the correct format",False,True
