----------------------
# CVPR25 and CLEF25 Context

This competition is held jointly as part of:

the [LifeCLEF 2025 lab](https://www.imageclef.org/LifeCLEF2025) of the [CLEF 2025](https://clef2025.clef-initiative.eu/index.php) conference, and of
the [FGVC12 workshop](https://sites.google.com/view/fgvc12/home) organized in conjunction with [CVPR 2025 conference](https://cvpr.thecvf.com/).
Being part of scientific research, the participants are encouraged to participate to both events. In particular, only participants who submitted a working note paper to LifeCLEF (see below) will be part of the officially published ranking used for scientific communication.

FGVC12 at CVPR 2025
This competition is part of the Fine-Grained Visual Categorization FGVC12 workshop in June at the Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition Conference CVPR 2025. The task results will be presented at the workshop, and the contribution of the winning team(s) will be highlighted. Attending the workshop is not required to participate in the competition.

CVPR 2025 will take place in Hashville, USA, on June 11-15, 2025.
PLEASE NOTE: CVPR frequently sells out early; we cannot guarantee CVPR registration after the competition's end. If you are interested in attending, please plan ahead.

You can see a list of the FGVC12 competitions [here](https://sites.google.com/view/fgvc11/competitions).

LifeCLEF 2025 at CLEF 2025
LifeCLEF lab is part of the Conference and Labs of the Evaluation Forum (CLEF).
CLEF consists of independent peer-reviewed workshops on a broad range of challenges in multilingual and multimodal information access evaluation and benchmarking activities in various labs designed to test different aspects of mono and cross-language Information retrieval systems.
CLEF 2025 will take place in Madrid, Spain, on September 9-12, 2025.
You can find more details on the CLEF 2025 [website](https://clef2025.clef-initiative.eu/).
