8910,beat-xgboost-with-neural-nets-smoker-status,"# Overview

**Welcome to the 2023 Kaggle Playground Series!** Thank you to everyone who participated in and contributed to Season 3 Playground Series so far! 

**Your Goal:** For this Episode of the Series, your task is to use binary classification to predict a patient's smoking status given information about various other health indicators. 

But here¡¯s the twist: alongside traditional models like XGBoost, we invite you to try out NdLinear ¡ª a new drop-in replacement for nn.Linear that improves generalization while reducing parameters, FLOPs, and memory. It works across MLPs, Transformers, RNNs, and more.

Get started here:
?? https://github.com/ensemble-core/NdLinear

?? Star the repo and test NdLinear in your neural network implementations ¡ª we¡¯d love to see creative approaches that challenge the usual tree-based baselines!

Good luck, and have fun experimenting!
----------------------
# Evaluation

Submissions are evaluated on [area under the ROC curve](http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Receiver_operating_characteristic) between the predicted probability and the observed target.


## Submission File
For each `id` in the test set, you must predict the probability for the target variable `smoking`. The file should contain a header and have the following format:

    id,smoking
    159256,0.5
    159257,0.5
    159258,0.5
    etc.",,False,True
