8988,delaware-student-discipline-dataset,"# Overview

The dataset for this competition comes from <a href=""https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/noeyislearning/delaware-student-discipline/data"">here</a>.

In order to prevent label leakage, a portion of the data has been sampled as the training and testing sets for this competition. Have a great time.
----------------------
# Description

This competition is a time series task that requires participants to predict the number of disciplinary actions taken by the school in the following year based on the disciplinary actions taken by students in previous years.

What needs to be predicted here is the data for 2023.


<a href=""https://www.kaggle.com/code/yunsuxiaozi/podsd2025-demo-submission"">Demo Submission</a>
----------------------
# Evaluation

```python
import numpy as np
def rmsle(y_true,y_pred):
    return np.sqrt(np.mean((np.log1p(y_true)-np.log1p(y_pred))**2))
```","# Dataset Description

About Dataset
This dataset provides detailed information on student disciplinary actions in Delaware schools, categorized by various demographic groups such as race, gender, grade level, and special demographics. The data includes the number of students receiving disciplinary actions, the total number of incidents, the average duration of disciplinary actions, and the percentage of students receiving disciplinary actions relative to overall enrollment. The dataset is essential for understanding disciplinary trends, identifying patterns, and informing interventions in Delaware's educational system.",False,True
