9009,detect-ai-vs-human-generated-images,"# Overview

**Can You Tell the Difference?**

In today¡¯s rapidly evolving digital landscape, AI-generated content is becoming more sophisticated and widespread. From deep-fakes to generative art, distinguishing between what¡¯s real and what¡¯s AI is a growing challenge with profound implications for media, security, and creativity.


This competition invites you to design machine learning models that can accurately classify images as AI-generated or human-created, while ensuring fairness and robust performance across a diverse dataset.

To participate to this challenge and win our prizes register your team on the official **Women in AI** page: https://www.womeninai.co/kagglechallenge2025


----------------------
# Description

The rise of generative AI has brought remarkable advancements in creating realistic images, videos, and audio. However, with this progress comes the challenge of distinguishing between authentic human-created content and AI-generated content, particularly in the context of deepfakes. Deepfake detection has become a critical area of research due to its implications for media trust, security, and ethics. Misuse of generative AI can lead to the spread of misinformation, erosion of public trust, and potential harm to individuals and institutions.

The dataset for this challenge, provided by Shutterstock and DeepMedia, combines authentic and AI-generated images to create a robust foundation for training and evaluation. Authentic images are sourced from Shutterstock's platform, including a balanced selection where one-third of the images feature humans. These are paired with their AI-generated counterparts, created by DeepMedia using state-of-the-art generative models. This pairing ensures a direct comparison between real and AI-generated content, enhancing model training and enabling the development of robust image authenticity detection systems.

**The complete dataset with the images is available for download here:** **https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/alessandrasala79/ai-vs-human-generated-dataset**

Below are some examples from the dataset, illustrating authentic images paired with their generated text labels and AI-generated equivalents:

![](https://www.googleapis.com/download/storage/v1/b/kaggle-user-content/o/inbox%2F8508630%2F62fa0a15d9505f1fc547c17261ea2deb%2Ftrain_1c6f648cd6323030e1b818776462c10e_real_right.jpg?generation=1736543742114260&alt=media)

![](https://www.googleapis.com/download/storage/v1/b/kaggle-user-content/o/inbox%2F8508630%2F874c15e7181c572ebd774dd13a5f7b49%2Ftrain_1f72bfb3cb4d30d2179aa67f1b2f81f8_real_right.jpg?generation=1736543882907432&alt=media)

![](https://www.googleapis.com/download/storage/v1/b/kaggle-user-content/o/inbox%2F8508630%2F391412145a6e42fa3796f617a91148ad%2Ftrain_1dd9f2b3a61fcce0a1082ad3fcf9a442_real_right.jpg?generation=1736544173193156&alt=media)

## Why Participate?

- **Real-World Impact**: Tackle the challenge of deepfake detection, a critical issue for media authenticity and security.
- **Skill Development**: Gain hands-on experience with dataset from industry leaders.
- **Global Recognition**: Compete with data scientists worldwide and showcase your work.
- **Inclusivity**: Be part of a challenge that promotes diversity and fairness in AI.

----------------------
# Timeline

- **Competition Launch:** Jan 15th 
- **Final Submission Deadline:** March 7th 
- **Winners Announced:** March 14th 

All deadlines are at 11:59 PM UTC.
----------------------
# Prizes

The total prize pool for this competition is $10,000, distributed as follows:

- 1st Place:  Best Innovative Team  
$2,000 cash prize for the team
WAI Challenge award certificate for each team member
- 2nd Place: Best Student Team
$2,000 cash prize for the team
WAI Challenge award certificate for each team member
- 3rd Place: Best Diverse Team
$2,000 cash prize for the team
WAI Challenge award certificate for each team member
- 4th Place: Best Female Team
$2,000 cash prize for the team
WAI Challenge award certificate for each team member
- 5th Place: Best Global South Team
$2,000 cash prize for the team
WAI Challenge award certificate for each team member

Prizes will be awarded based on two key criteria:

- Leaderboard Ranking: The top-performing teams, based on the quality of their models, will be recognised for their technical achievements.

- Innovation and diversity: In addition to performance, teams that demonstrate diversity in gender, ethnicity, and nationality will be acknowledged and celebrated for contributing to a more inclusive AI community.

Ensure you sign up [here](https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLScWbIDqcMqGfs2b5TLloYSUv0DoigUVtkfB84V6sHZFI-w7Vg/viewform) . This allows us capture your team¡¯s diversity and ensures you are eligible for the prizes. We believe in rewarding both innovation and inclusivity, driving meaningful change in AI.
----------------------
# Registration

All participants are required to register with Women in AI. For team participation, only team leaders are required to complete the registration form on behalf of their teams, indicating the team name.

- **Register Here (Individuals and Team Leaders Only)**: [Click to Register](https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLScWbIDqcMqGfs2b5TLloYSUv0DoigUVtkfB84V6sHZFI-w7Vg/viewform)
- **Register Team Composition Here (All other Team Members)**: [Click to Register](https://docs.google.com/forms/d/1ACGoQpKHYcg9Upr5lnvkR6HgDwFPtY4WPQi07f5GdGE/preview)
----------------------
# Evaluation 

Submissions are evaluated on the following criteria:

?	Primary Metric: The competition¡¯s primary evaluation metric is the F1-Score, which balances precision and recall to measure your model¡¯s effectiveness in identifying AI-generated and human-created images. It is calculated at the 0.5 threshold. 

## Submission Format

Participants must submit their predictions in the specified format to be eligible for evaluation. Please follow the guidelines below to ensure your submission is valid:

1. **Test file**: Provided in the Data section as `test.csv`
2. **File Format**: Submissions should be in a CSV file format.
3. **Columns**:
   - The file must contain only two columns:
     - **id**: A unique identifier for each test image.
     - **label**: The predicted class for each image (e.g., 0 for human-created and 1 for AI-generated).
   - Any additional columns or index columns should be removed before submission.

Example Format:

    id,label
    1,0
    2,1
    3,0
    4,1
    etc.

## Notebook Requirements

In addition to the prediction file:

- Submitted notebooks should be **clear, well-documented, and easily replicable**.
- Ensure that:
  - **Code is structured and annotated** to facilitate understanding.
  - **Results are reproducible** when the notebook is executed with the provided dataset.

Submissions that lack clarity or fail to meet reproducibility standards may not be considered for final evaluation.

