# Team Formation

At Women in AI, we believe in fostering collaboration and diversity in AI by creating opportunities for individuals to work together on meaningful challenges. The AI vs. Human-Generated Images Challenge encourages participants to form teams and leverage the power of teamwork to tackle a real-world problem in AI and machine learning.

### Team Formation Guidelines
- The challenge is open to **individuals or teams of up to 4 participants**.
- **Diversity matters!** While there are no specific gender requirements, we encourage the inclusion of underrepresented groups in AI to ensure diverse perspectives and solutions.
- Once you join a team on Kaggle, you cannot remove yourself or switch to another team, so choose wisely!

### Suggestions for Forming Teams
- **Post in the Discussion Forums**: Use the Kaggle discussion boards to connect with other participants looking for teammates.
- **Connect via Social Media**: Share your interest in the challenge on LinkedIn, Twitter, or other platforms and look for others interested in forming a team.
- **Collaborate Locally**: Reach out to colleagues, peers, or AI communities near you to build a team with complementary skills.

### Why Form a Team?
- **Leverage Diverse Skills**: A team with varied skill sets can tackle different aspects of the competition more effectively.
- **Learn Together**: Collaborate, exchange ideas, and grow your data science and AI skills with others.
- **Build Connections**: Networking with team members and the wider community is an invaluable part of the competition experience.

Whether you¡¯re participating solo or with a team, this challenge is a chance to connect, learn, and create an impactful solution.

----------------------
# Acknowledgements

We extend our heartfelt gratitude to our partners and sponsors who have made the AI vs. Human-Generated Images Challenge possible. Their contributions are vital in empowering participants and advancing innovation in AI.

- **Shutterstock**  
  As a global leader in creative content, Shutterstock has provided a rich dataset of high-quality, human-created images. These images form the backbone of the competition, ensuring participants work with diverse and authentic content.

- **DeepMedia**  
  DeepMedia has generously contributed cutting-edge AI-generated image datasets, challenging participants to develop solutions that reflect real-world complexities. Their expertise in AI-generated content adds depth and relevance to the challenge.

