9030,fungi-clef-2025,"# Overview

The FungiCLEF Challenge focuses on few-shot recognition of fungi species using real-world observational data. Each observation includes multiple photographs of the same specimen, along with metadata (e.g., location, timestamp, substrate, habitat, toxicity), satellite imagery and meteorological variables.

The goal of the challenge is to develop a classification model capable of returning a ranked list of predicted species for each observation. A key challenge lies in handling a large number of species consisted of rare and under-recorded taxa with very few training examples.

**Input**: A list of fungi observations.
**Output**: A list of Top-k predicted fungi species from a predefined set of classes.

----------------------
# Motivation

Automatic recognition of fungi species aids mycologists, citizen scientists, and nature enthusiasts in identifying species in the wild while supporting the collection of valuable biodiversity data. To be effective on a large scale, such as in popular citizen science projects, it needs to efficiently predict species with limited resources and handle many classes, some of which have just a few recorded observations. Additionally, rare species are often excluded from training, making it difficult for AI-powered tools to recognize them.

Based on our measurements, we recognized that about 20% of all verified observations (20,000) involve rare or under-recorded species, highlighting the need to accurately identify these species.
----------------------
# Timeline

- **December 2024**: [Registration opens for all LifeCLEF challenges (free of charge)] (https://clef2025-labs-registration.dei.unipd.it/registrationForm.php)
- **7 March 2025**: Competition Start
- ~~12 May 2025~~ **19 May 2025**: Competition Deadline
- ~~31 May 2025~~ **7 June 2025**: Deadline for submission of working note papers by participants [CEUR-WS proceedings]
- **23 June 2025**: Notification of acceptance - working note papers [CEUR-WS proceedings].
- **30 June 2025**: Camera-ready deadline for working note papers.
- **9-12 Sept 2025**: CLEF 2025 Madrid - Spain.

_All deadlines are at 11:59 PM CET of the corresponding day unless otherwise stated._ 

**The competition organizers reserve the right to update the contest timeline if they deem it necessary.**
----------------------
# Evaluation metrics

The evaluation metrics for this competition is the standard Recall@k which is defined as the proportion of instances where the true label is within the top \\(k\\) predicted labels:
$$
\text{Top-k Accuracy} = \frac{\sum_{i=1}^N \mathbb{1}(y_i \in \hat{Y}_i^k)}{N},
$$
where \\(N\\) is the total number of samples, \\(y_i\\) is the true label for the \\(i\\)-th sample, \\(\hat{Y}_i^k\\) is the set of top \\(k\\) predicted labels for the \\(i\\)-th sample, and \\(\mathbb{1}(\cdot)\\) is the indicator function.

We set  \\(k=5\\) for the main evaluation metric.

# Submission format
For each ObservationId in the test set, you must predict 10 species. The submission file is a CSV containing two columns for each sample (row):
*   `observationId` column containing integers corresponding to the test sample ids
*   `predictions` column containing space-delimited lists of the predicted species identifiers (speciesId in training/validation datasets)
```
observationId,predictions
3305985310, 307 508 101 203 999 453 312 876 431 289
3305985311, 597 123 430 802 76 918 212 345 567 890
3305985312, 1060 42 785 222 308 654 732 907 304 409
...
```

While the evaluation metric is Recall@5, top 10 predictions are required to facilitate further analysis.

----------------------
# Other Resources

For more FungiCLEF-related info, please refer to overview papers from previous editions.
- **Dataset Paper** describing used data --> [FungiTastic](https://arxiv.org/pdf/2408.13632) 
- Papers describing the old dataset [Danish Fungi dataset] (https://openaccess.thecvf.com/content/WACV2022/html/Picek_Danish_Fungi_2020_-_Not_Just_Another_Image_Recognition_Dataset_WACV_2022_paper.html) and our [Fungi Recognition App](https://www.mdpi.com/1424-8220/22/2/633).
-  [FungiCLEF2024 Overview Paper](https://ceur-ws.org/Vol-3740/paper-185.pdf), [FungiCLEF2023 Overview Paper](https://ceur-ws.org/Vol-3497/paper-165.pdf), and [FungiCLEF2022 Overview Paper](https://ceur-ws.org/Vol-3180/paper-157.pdf).

Besides, you can check out other competitions from the CLEF-LifeCLEF and CVPR-FGVC workshops.
- [LifeCLEF](https://www.imageclef.org/LifeCLEF2025) page for more information about LifeCLEF challenges and working notes submission procedure.
- [CVPR - FGVC12 workshop](https://sites.google.com/view/fgvc12) page for more information about the FGVC12 workshop.
----------------------
# CVPR25 and CLEF25 Context

**This competition is held jointly as part of:**

- the [LifeCLEF 2025](https://www.imageclef.org/LifeCLEF2025) lab of the [CLEF 2025](http://clef2025.clef-initiative.eu) conference, and of
