9164,nek-310-lecture-12,"# Overview

The task is to fit two models, one logistic regression and one other model of your choice, to predict the probability of credit default.
----------------------
# Description

When building a good prediction model it may be the case that you can get a better if you first do som feature engineering, derive new potential explanatory variables from ""the raw ones"". For the credit default data some ""engineered delinquency variable"" may turn out to be a stronger risk driver than the ones found using just the raw data.
----------------------
# Evaluation

Without proper self-evaluation, failure is inevitable.","# Dataset Description

There are 25 variables:

ID: ID of each client
LIMIT_BAL: Amount of given credit in NT dollars (includes individual and family/supplementary credit
SEX: Gender (1=male, 2=female)
EDUCATION: (1=graduate school, 2=university, 3=high school, 4=others, 5=unknown, 6=unknown)
MARRIAGE: Marital status (1=married, 2=single, 3=others)
AGE: Age in years
PAY_0: Repayment status in September, 2023 (-1=pay duly, 1=payment delay for one month, 2=payment delay for two months, ¡­ 8=payment delay for eight months, 9=payment delay for nine months and above)
PAY_2: Repayment status in August, 2023 (scale same as above)
PAY_3: Repayment status in July, 2023 (scale same as above)
PAY_4: Repayment status in June, 2023 (scale same as above)
PAY_5: Repayment status in May, 2023 (scale same as above)
PAY_6: Repayment status in April, 2023 (scale same as above)
BILL_AMT1: Amount of bill statement in September, 2023 (NT dollar)
BILL_AMT2: Amount of bill statement in August, 2023 (NT dollar)
BILL_AMT3: Amount of bill statement in July, 2023 (NT dollar)
BILL_AMT4: Amount of bill statement in June, 2023 (NT dollar)
BILL_AMT5: Amount of bill statement in May, 2023 (NT dollar)
BILL_AMT6: Amount of bill statement in April, 2023 (NT dollar)
PAY_AMT1: Amount of previous payment in September, 2023 (NT dollar)
PAY_AMT2: Amount of previous payment in August, 2023 (NT dollar)
PAY_AMT3: Amount of previous payment in July, 2023 (NT dollar)
PAY_AMT4: Amount of previous payment in June, 2023 (NT dollar)
PAY_AMT5: Amount of previous payment in May, 2023 (NT dollar)
PAY_AMT6: Amount of previous payment in April, 2023 (NT dollar)
default.payment.next.month: Default payment (1=yes, 0=no)

THERE MAY BE SOME DIRT IN THE DATA, that may have to be taken care of...",False,True
