# AG-VPReID 2025 Competition
## The Second Aerial-Ground Person Re-identification Challenge

Welcome to AG-VPReID 2025, the second installment of the Aerial-Ground Person Re-identification Challenge series! This competition addresses the critical challenge of matching individuals between aerial drone footage and ground-level cameras¡ªa crucial capability for modern surveillance systems, security applications, and public safety operations.

### The Challenge

Person re-identification (ReID) involves matching individuals across non-overlapping camera views. While ground-based ReID has been extensively researched, aerial-ground ReID¡ªespecially at high altitudes¡ªremains largely unexplored due to unique challenges:

- Extreme viewpoint differences between aerial (80-120m altitude) and ground cameras
- Significant scale variations and resolution disparities
- Motion blur and occlusions in dynamic aerial footage
- Diverse environmental conditions and illumination changes

### The Dataset

AG-VPReID is a novel large-scale dataset featuring:
- 3,027 identities (including 1,693 distractors)
- 13,507 tracklets with approximately 3.7 million frames
- Video data captured from drones at high altitudes (80-120m)
- Multiple ground camera perspectives (CCTV and wearable cameras)
- 15 soft-biometric attributes annotated for each identity

### Your Goal

Your challenge is to develop robust algorithms for video-based person re-identification between high-altitude aerial footage and ground-level cameras. Participants will train models to accurately match individuals across these drastically different viewpoints, leveraging both spatial and temporal information in the video sequences.

### Evaluation Metrics

Performance will be evaluated using:
- Mean Average Precision (mAP)1
- Cumulative Matching Characteristics (CMC)2 at Rank-1, Rank-5, and Rank-10
- Altitude-specific metrics to assess robustness across different flying heights

### Important Dates
- Competition Start: March 2025
- Competition End: June 3, 2025
- Winners Announcement: By June 23, 2025

This competition is organized in conjunction with the International Joint Conference on Biometrics (IJCB) 2025.

Join us in pushing the boundaries of cross-view person re-identification and developing solutions for this challenging real-world surveillance scenario!

