## Data Structure
- Each video tracklet: `{ID}/{Tracklet}/{Image/Frame}`
- Frame format e.g P81T2310171A2C2E152K7F7528 breaks down as:
- P81: Person identifier for collection day only (not permanent ID)
- T231017: Collection date (Oct 17, 2023)
- 1A2: Altitude indicator (A2 = 80m, A3 = 120m)
- C2: Camera type (C0-C6 representing CCTVx2/GoProx2/UAVx2)
- E152: Event identifier (for annotation purpose)
- K7: Key point reference (for annotation purpose)
- F7528: Frame number from video

## Files Description
- `train/` - Training tracklets organized by person ID
- `attributes/` - 15 soft-biometric attributes (CSV format) for train and testing cases

### Testing Case 1: Aerial to Ground
- `case1_aerial_to_ground_query/` - Query tracklets
- `case1_aerial_to_ground_gallery/` - Gallery tracklets

### Testing Case 2: Ground to Aerial
- `case2_ground_to_aerial_query/` - Query tracklets
- `case2_ground_to_aerial_gallery/` - Gallery tracklets

