9271,synthetic-2-real-object-detection-challenge,"# Overview

# Synthetic to Real Object Detection Challenge ??

### ?? Challenge Summary  
Welcome to the **Synthetic-to-Real Object Detection Challenge**!  In this challenge, participants compete to get the best real-world object detection results while training their model with **100% synthetic data**. This competition is based on **real-world AI applications** where models trained in controlled virtual environments must perform well in complex, unseen conditions.


Participants will train a model on **synthetic soup can images** generated in [Falcon](http://duality.ai/edu?utm_source=kaggle&utm_medium=kaggle_competition&utm_campaign=competition_1), Duality AI¡¯s digital twin simulation software, and then test the model¡¯s performance on previously **unseen real-world images**. The twist? **You can boost your score by creating your own digital twin-based synthetic data with Falcon! [Create an account here to start learning how.](https://falcon.duality.ai/secure/documentation?learnWelcome=true&sidebarMode=learn&utm_source=kaggle&utm_medium=kaggle_competition&utm_campaign=competition_1)**   

**What's In it for you?**  
- **Win prizes**: Cash awards, Certificates and Shoutouts on platforms like LinkedIn and Hugging Face with a chance to feature on our competition blog.  
- **Master synthetic data**: Learn skills applicable to real-world AI deployment.  
- **Boost your portfolio**: Showcase your AI & ML skills in real-world object detection.
- **[Free Falcon EDU access](http://duality.ai/edu?utm_source=kaggle&utm_medium=kaggle_competition&utm_campaign=competition_1)**: Hands-on experience with high-fidelity synthetic data generation tools.  
- **Stand out to recruiters**: Rank high on Kaggle, build credibility, and showcase your skills on LinkedIn, GitHub, and resumes.
- **[Network & grow](https://discord.com/invite/dualityfalconcommunity)**: Compete with fellow students, ML engineers, researchers, collaborating on our Discord to answer questions and build connections.

So, how well can your model **detect objects in real-world images after training only on synthetic data**? Let¡¯s find out!   

---

### ?? **Objective**
- **Train on synthetic data**: Use our synthetic dataset or **[generate your own with Falcon](https://falcon.duality.ai/secure/documentation/ex-1-objdetection?sidebarMode=learn&utm_source=kaggle&utm_medium=kaggle_competition&utm_campaign=competition_1)**.  
- **Test on real-world images**: Detect a soup can in real-world images. 
- **Score using mAP@50**: Achieve the highest **mAP@50** (Mean Average Precision at IoU 0.5) score.   

---

### ?? **Why Synthetic Data?**
Synthetic data is **cost-effective, scalable, and bias-free** ¨C yet synthetic-trained models often fail in real-world conditions  (referred to as the Sim2Real gap). Since 2018 [Duality] (https://www.duality.ai/?utm_source=kaggle&utm_medium=kaggle_competition&utm_campaign=competition_1) has been building tools and strategies that bridge this gap, and we¡¯re sharing them with you! 

[Check out our main simulation tool, FalconEditor, via any of the cloud-based simulations available on our page!](https://falcon.duality.ai/secure/scenarios?utm_source=kaggle&utm_medium=kaggle_competition&utm_campaign=competition_1)

The skills you develop in this challenge apply to: 

- Autonomous robots 
- Industrial automation  
- AI-driven quality control  
- Augmented reality (AR) & Computer Vision applications
- And many more cutting-edge technologies!

**Featured Tool**: [Falcon Editor](http://duality.ai/edu?utm_source=kaggle&utm_medium=kaggle_competition&utm_campaign=competition_1)  
- Free subscription tier available, Sign up [here](https://falcon.duality.ai/secure/documentation/ex-1-objdetection?sidebarMode=learn&utm_source=kaggle&utm_medium=kaggle_competition&utm_campaign=competition_1)   
- Generates 400+ high-quality synthetic images in minutes  
- Customize lighting, angles, occlusions, and camera viewpoints  
- See example FalconEditor scenarios [here on our user site](https://falcon.duality.ai/secure/scenarios?utm_source=kaggle&utm_medium=kaggle_competition&utm_campaign=competition_1)
----------------------
# Description

## ?? **About This Challenge**
####**What You Need to Do**
Participants will **train a model** on **synthetic images** and the trained model will then **predict bounding boxes** for real-world test images.  
The model¡¯s performance is evaluated based on **mAP@50** (Mean Average Precision at IoU 0.5).   

---

## **?? How to Get Started**
1. **Download the dataset** from the ""[Data](https://www.kaggle.com/competitions/synthetic-2-real-object-detection-challenge/data)"" tab.
2. **Set up your environment**:
   - **Local**: Follow the Environment Setup guide in this section below.
3. **Fetch the sample dataset training, prediction, and csv conversion scripts** to get started.
4. **Note:** Make sure the yaml file has the correct locations of the train, val, and test folders
5. **Train a YOLOv8 model** on the synthetic dataset using our `train.py` script.  
6. **Run predictions on test images** using `predict.py` to output a labels folder.
7. **Convert the labels in .txt to a submission.csv** with our `convert_to_csv.py` file and then submit the csv file.
8. **Confirm the format of your predictions** are correct using the submission format described in the [Evaluation Section](www.kaggle.com/competitions/synthetic-2-real-object-detection-challenge/overview/evaluation).
9. **Check the [leaderboard](https://www.kaggle.com/competitions/synthetic-2-real-object-detection-challenge/leaderboard)** to see how your model performs in comparison to other competitors!
10. **Join the [Discord Community](https://discord.com/invite/dualityfalconcommunity)** for solving queries related to the competition in the `kaggle-competitions` channel.

---

## ?? **Environment Setup**

### Prerequisites
Ensure you have either of the following installed:
- [Anaconda](https://www.anaconda.com/) 
- [Miniconda](https://docs.conda.io/en/latest/miniconda.html)

### Installation Steps

#### 1. Install Dependencies
Run the provided batch file in ENV_SETUP to set up the Conda environment:
```sh
setup_env.bat
```
This will:
- Create a new Conda environment named **`EDU`**.

#### 2. Activate the Environment. 
```sh
   conda activate EDU
```
- This will install Python 3.10 and the following packages
  - `ultralytics`
  - `opencv-python`
  - `PyYAML`
  - `opencv-contrib-python`

**Note**: If your computer has problems with the conda commands try using the anaconda prompt window for step 2.

---

## **Running the Code**
Once the environment is set up, activate the EDU environment using `conda activate EDU` and navigate to the directory containing the scripts:

### 1. **Train the Model**
```sh
python train.py
```
### 2. **Make Predictions on the Test Images**
```sh
python predict.py
```
### 3. **Convert Predictions to a CSV file for Submission**
```sh
python convert_preds_to_csv.py
```

---

