Welcome to the next phase of *Operation Sky Watchman*. In this task, you will go beyond inference by training and testing a YOLOv11 model. Your objective is to adjust key hyperparameters and evaluate how these changes affect the model's ability to detect aircrafts.
----------------------
# Description

#### Mission Briefing: Training the Guards
Your task is to fine-tune a YOLOv11 model using a provided dataset with two classes - both labeled as 'airplane.' You will experiment with different versions of YOLOv11 (nano, medium, large,...) and optimize hyperparameters such as the number of epochs, batch size, and learning rate. The goal is to strike a balance between detection accuracy and efficiency.

#### Why Hyperparameters Matter
Hyperparameters are key settings that control how a machine learning model learns from data. Adjusting these parameters impacts both the model's accuracy and the time it takes to train. This task will teach you how to train models, interpret performance metric (like mAP), and understand the trade-offs involved in optimizing an AI system.

#### Your Mission Objectives
1. Select a YOLOv11 model variant (e.g., nano, medium, or large).
2. Adjust hyperparameters (e.g., epochs, batch size, learning rate) to train the model.
3. Evaluate your model's performance using the mAP@50 metric.
4. Submit your predictions and monitor your position on the leaderboard.
----------------------
# Evaluation

Similar to task 1, the score will based on mAP@50.","# Dataset Description

