9281,smallest-representation-of-a-dataset-what-is-it,"# Overview

The vast world we see is governed by tiny yet universal forces (from atoms to planets, from algebraic groups to equations of degree 5 or greater, etc.). And so, is it too much to say that the task of science is to explore the beauty of these tiny forces through the lens of truth, shaped by the smallness of human existence and the overwhelmingness of unanswered questions?

The above thoughts will be materialized in this competition to emphasize it further, so that data science focuses on a crucial question that cannot be ignored: *Can you find a minimal set that represents these 10,000 data points?*

**Your Goal:** Find a minimal set, also called the *representative set*, that represents all 10,000 data points. Good luck!

